{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting","id":837964,"title":"How do you Hack your Setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-26T23:52:02-08:00","id":837964,"title":"How do you Hack your Setting?","content":"Everybody knows that, whether you call yourself a games master, a story teller, a dungeon keeper, whatever, if you're playing an RPG, you're likely to customize it. And with fluff and themes that can often be highly contentious, the Chronicles of Darkness are no exception to that rule. Since there's a whole bunch of threads scattered over these boards discussing different ways of making specific setting hacks work, I was wondering if anyone would be willing to share the ways they've tweaked and changed the Chronicles of Darkness to make them truly <i>theirs</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully not being rude here, my own answer to my question...<br /> <br /> For starters, I run my Chronicles of Darkness closer to Dark Urban Fantasy than pure Horror. There's still some horror in it, hence the &quot;dark&quot; part of that descriptor, but exactly what is horrifying and how much so depends on lot on where you're standing.<br /> <br /> The general approach to the setting is inspired by Unknown Armies, and can be summed up in two words: Occult Underground. The world humanity thinks it lives in is but the tip of the iceberg, and things get darker and scarier the deeper you dare to descend into the shadows. Past the Requiem Sanguine of the vampires, down through the hellish worlds of the spirits, the fae and the dead, past the resentful fragments of old gods and new, deeper and deeper until you reach the layer where beings of divine might conduct a subtly fought eternal war that ever threatens to tear the fabric of reality itself apart.<br /> <br /> From a mortal perspective, the setting has something of a Cosmic Horror motif, for a simple reason: Humanity Does Not Matter. I agree that the Old World of Darkness went too far with its description of the power and influence of supernaturals, but at the same time, I feel that the New World pulls too many of their fangs for my liking. My Chronicles have it that monsters aren't as a general rule, controlling everything - but that's because, as a general rule, they have better things to do. Mages examine mysteries that could redefine reality as humans know it. Vampires whirl away the eternity with feeding and intercine strife. Werewolves hunt ceaseless, as incapable of conceiving of an alternative as they are of physically stopping. Whatever problems monsters have with humanity is on a localized, individual level; across the world as a whole, what happens to humanity bothers supernaturals not a whit.<br /> <br /> This, then, gives Hunters a somewhat darker motif. Yes, the Vigil is a candle in the dark... but the thing about candles? <i>They burn out</i>. Pyrrhic victories, bittersweet endings, and the nagging query of &quot;is this really worth it?&quot; are the order of the day. Of course, a world is only dark if there is light to contrast it; many hunters do decide that, yes, this <b>is</b> worth it, and taking whatever victories you can is part of the theme as well.<br /> <br /> As you might guess, I make a significant use of Imperial Mysteries as a basis for &quot;the god tier&quot; of the Chronicles of Darkness, painting the higher worlds and the manifold powers who must meddle subtly, lest they unmake the world in their enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> Something inspired by a setting hack actually here in the Mage forum now, my setting has more Watchtowers than the core five. The core five are just the most common; every imaginable tripartite combination has its representative Watchtower. This alters the effect of False Awakening (Night Horrors: The Unbidden) slightly, with those rare scholars of the arcane who know of the Archmages wondering if it mightn't have been a failed gambit by an Archmage... or, worse, if it mightn't have somehow retroactively created the &quot;lesser watchtowers&quot; as equivalent exchange for burning itself into creation.<br /> <br /> There are a few other bits and pieces, but these are the main hacks I apply to my setting. So, what're yours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T01:36:56-08:00","id":837977,"title":"","content":"The big hack I've used most has been combining the Shadow and the Astral. I've only used that in mortal games, so it's not really something I needed to coherently flesh out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T03:39:12-08:00","id":837990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=837977#post837977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big hack I've used most has been combining the Shadow and the Astral. I've only used that in mortal games, so it's not really something I needed to coherently flesh out.</div> </div> </div> </div> You may not have fleshed it out, but could you give a general description of how that worked? I'm intrigued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T11:05:33-08:00","id":838137,"title":"","content":"I hesitate because it was quite a few years back. Plus, I generally used basic guidelines in my head without actually creating any coherent cosmology to go with it. I broadly speaking knew what I wanted and just kinda went with that.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think in retrospect it basically resembled the Umbra from WoD but built using the elements of CofD. So the realm (I actually deliberately didn't have the NPCs give it a name) mirrored the material world, but there was a lot of it that didn't (I guess those exist in the Shadow as written but this was on a much bigger scale), and the structure for travelling it resembled the Astral in the way that you had to think your way to other places, but on the otherhand, it was still a lot more coherent than the dream logic of the Astral. It was also possible to reach 'sub-realms' that didn't correspond with anything on Earth, but were closer to realms such as Alkhest where ideas are represented in metaphor.<br /> <br /> Sorry I can't be more helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:53:23-08:00","id":838179,"title":"","content":"Well, first off, everything <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\">here</a>. Especially the setting hack docs for the assorted lines.<br /> <br /> Beyond that I have some general setting rules I tend to go by:<ul><li>I've downplayed the X-Splats in every game I could. Vampires use Bloodlines, Werewolves shift Auspice, a Mage's Path only serves to describe his general world view, etc. Same with Y-Splats, though to a lesser degree. It's not a fair assumption to assume all cities have the big five Covenants represented (indeed, it's very rare), or that Tribes are world-spanning groups. Basically all changes are intended to reduce the sense of a homogenous global community, and encourage distinct regional settings and quirks.</li> <li>I removed most of the &quot;formerly human, now pure evil&quot; counter-splats. Belial's Brood, The Pure, The Exarchs (and by extension the seers). That's not to say I removed asshole villains, only that those villains tend to come from within, and be individuals as opposed to groups. Individuals is a big deal when I run, all characters are themselves first and members of their respective groups second.<ul><li>Wholly alien threats, like the God-Machine, Gentry or Abyssal entities remain horrific, but in a &quot;they aren't evil, just completely different&quot; sort of way.</li> </ul></li> <li>Attached to the previous two points, Supernatural populations are kept very small. Mini-splats: Revenants, Wolf-Blooded, Fae Touched, etc. play a bigger role and greatly outnumber their major counterpart upwards of 100:1 (Sleepwalkers to Mages). This is primarily to keep the 'magic level' more down to earth, and make any character with a Major splat clearly, a big player. It also help manage NPCs on the fly, and prevent over-saturation of high-magical characters</li> <li>I downplay otherworldly travel in all games where it's relevant. When it does occur, it is dangerous and significant. Werewolves about to embark on a hunt in the shadow? Shit is going down. Astral journey to discover a lost truth? Story climax. All-in-all the aim is to keep the game here, on earth, and not strolling out into otherworldly superspace (which is something I associate more with cWoD).</li> <li>Mage, Demon and Geist see some fairly considerable changes.<ul><li><b>Mage: </b>Paths define little more than the Mage's version of Mage Sight, and color their view of reality. Mages have a harder time slinging Improvised spells (no Ruling Arcana), but Rotes are considerably stronger and easier to learn. I forwent Legacies for Arts, which serve much the same purpose but don't lock the Mage in as hard, so a Mage who wanted to spread out (and spend the experience) could learn several different &quot;styles&quot; of magic. All-in-all the aim is more style, less common, but more impactful spellcasting and an attempt to remove some of the sameyness between Mages of the same path.</li> <li><b>Demon: </b>Very little difference mechanically, but the God-Machine plays a much less active role. Demons are more free to act bizarre and use their powers, not quite openly, but with less fear of being hunted down and dragged back into the machine. Glitches now make up the primary repercussion for Cover loss, and most Demons are expected to have several Glitches.</li> <li><b>Geist: </b>Is hugely different, inspired by things like Persona, Jojo's Bizarre Adventure and (most recently) Ajin, Geister can manifest as ghostly forms and act on their host Sin-Eater's wishes. Manifestations are entirely custom to every character, evolving and developing into weird and unique abilities as they grow. Sin-Eater's labour under their Geist's passions, forced to enact them or fade from the memory as though they had actually died.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:17:29-08:00","id":838218,"title":"","content":"The mood is drawn from Delta Green and Unknown Armies; pursuit of the supernatural is something undertaken by the people determined/stupid/crazy enough not to keep their heads down like the rest of humanity, and they're punished for it. Hunter is particular is basically one big exercise in destroying your life in order to uphold the Vigil. Moral degredation is a big deal in Vampire and Hunter (what lengths will you go to in order to do what you have to - either to survive, or to fight back, respectively), and pretty much every game hinges on the horror of losing oneself, either to alien urges and ways of thinking, or jusy straight up sanity slippage. There's a sense of a secret history, though never in the form of &quot;Hitler was manipulated by Werewolves,&quot; instead focusing on the supernatural as a mirror to what the mortals are experiencing.<br /> <br /> Personal Horror, written in big letters on the front of every gamebook. I want to steer as clear from Urbam Fantasy as possible.<br /> <br /> As for more specific tweaks, my Mage antagonists are almost always drawn from the Pentacle itself, my God-Machine is either a work of Cold War occult science or else the Fallen mirror of the Principle, I've made some firm connections between Geist and Mummy, and I don't recognize Beast as part of my World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 02-27-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:30:54-08:00","id":838226,"title":"","content":"I've never really seen the need to change anything, the way the <i>CofD </i>is written really makes the sort of fleshing out people tend to do unnecessary, on-high connections that don't really interface with actual play (and, IMO, hurt the mystery of the setting, which the whole &quot;Darkness&quot; element is supposed to be based on.) I like to incorporate the various splats on the periphery of my games. Mage is one of the ones where you're most likely to see very random phenomena crop up, though Demon is another possible candidate. Otherwise they've generally got their own spheres of interest that don't often intersect. Beasts are actually pretty cool for this, though I haven't run a game with Beast PCs and I'm not sure I'm super interested in doing so.<br /> <br /> Vampires are pretty good at keeping the details under wraps, for example. So good in fact that they don't often run into the others.<br /> <br /> Their relationships are probably determined by different domains and stuff. My girlfriend is planning on running a Werewolf game in Toronto soon for instance, and it'll be interesting to see if she throws in any Changeling weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T16:49:33-08:00","id":838276,"title":"","content":"The last campaing I ran was Hunter: the Vigil, and usually when I run it, I modify the world heavily. I make full use of Dread Powers and great majority of my monsters are homebrewed. Even the &quot;official&quot; ones are heavily modified and do not exist as they do in their own books. I had silver-fearing daywalker vampires, sorcerous werefoxes, cultists and servant creatures of Alien God, cursed werewolf, strange cryptids formed by magical surges, witches of all sorts, ancient forest god/spirit, angels of Machine God and other sources, djinns, immortal relic hunter and many more. None of the creatures belonged to organisations described in books and most worked quite differently and with greatly reduced strength.<br /> <br /> I also didn't have Supernal Realms and spirits of Shadow Realm had much harder time affecting the world of flesh. &quot;God level&quot; creatures pretty much didn't exist or were unable to directly affect the world, and had to use mortal or supernatural agents. Mood was far closer to Urban Fantasy than Horror but terrible things happened and characters suffered from their calling (and from stupid choices). Still, hope burned bright and torch was kept lit, with some monsters being allies and others enemies. Supernatural world was far more splintered and varied than the one in books; surprisingly common relics, spontaneous magic surges and alternate universes &amp; other worlds creating unexplained, frightening and intriguing phenomena around the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","user":"Crazy_Ivan","date":". 02-27-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T07:12:19-08:00","id":838629,"title":"","content":"My biggest changes, mechanically, have been to Vampire, both Requiem and Masquerade. Thanks to the Translation guide, it started me off on a cool meld idea,and it just kind of snowballed.<br /> <br /> The initial hack was to use Generation and Blood Potency at the same time. Generation acts as a starting minimum and maximum potential boundary setter. Blood Potency increases with age, up to the maximum allowed by Generation. Then, remembering a line from the old Masquerade game about vampires hitting a thousand years old underoing a kind of change, I decided that any vampire who hits 1,000 can raise his upper limit by one for every thousand years he's alive. So if a 9th - 13th gen actually made it to 2,000 years old, he'd effectively be 7th Gen (because the maximum for those gens are all 5)<br /> <br /> While working on that, I realized, watching some related media, that I was never very fond of &quot;The Beast&quot;. So I replaced it with &quot;The Hunger.&quot; Instead of having to constantly worry about frenzy and rotshreck, a vampire instead has to make an effort of will to pull off a victim when feeding. They also gain a new stated called &quot;Hungry&quot;if their Blood Pool is less than half full. Normally, in my games, vamps all have Blush of life when sated, and when they get Hungry, they start to degrade.At Hungry, they look like classic WoD vamps, pale, cold to the touch, no pulse. At 1/4 or less, they gain &quot;Starving&quot;, and start to look more like Cappadocians. Each state has penalties to the Hunger checks when feeding. A botch means they go on a feeding rampage.<br /> <br /> Without rotschreck, I ditched sunlight and fire as Aggravated damage. Oh it'll still KILL them, they can just heal it. It also allows vampires, under certain conditions, to move about in daylight, something most can do in RL lore (as opposed to in-game lore). Aggravated damage is now caused solely by supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> After doing this, I realized the last great inequality of vampires versus every other supernatural. They have very few passive abilities, and those are tied to the three physical disciplines. So, I gave them a mild regenerative effect. As long as they're not &quot;Hungry&quot;, a vampire slowly repairs Bashed and Lethal damaged over time. Every turn, the highest level of damage downgrades. Lethal becomes Bashing. Bashing becomes healed. Aggravated damage can ONLY be cured by actively spending blood, and it's still limited to one a day. Remember, in my verse, a vampire is functionally &quot;alive&quot; as long as they're well-fed. Makes it harder for hunters to find them, too.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this can downplay the whole &quot;personal horror&quot; aspect, but I like to think it's preserved with the following conundrum. Whenever a vampire feeds, he risks killing. Period. No more &quot;i'm a noble vampire who never kills when I feed&quot; stuff. To stay alive, you have to eat. OFTEN. So more risk of killing. You can not eat as often, but you'll lose that warmth of humanity, and gain a higher risk of losing control when feeding. So which is less monstrous?<br /> <br /> I'm currently working on a homebrew setting,where I'm making it my own, partially by taking ideas from other shows, movies, and fiction, filing the serial numbers off, and merging them together into their own world.<br /> <br /> * Vampire - modified to be more like The Originals, with a bit of Blade. Clans are gone, in favor of player-created Bloodlines, reflecting regional lineages that hold sway in an area.<br /> * Werewolf - half Forsaken, half inspired by Bitten; the Forsaken are bitten, cursed werewolves, used as pawns by the Pure, who are natural born , aristocratic werewolves who breed true. Both guard the spirit world, but for different reasons.<br /> * Mage - thanks to the Dresden Files, I chucked the lore entirely, and replaced the factions with magical styles. The Council still exists, but as a kind of judicial body, mixed with dispute management. Their arch enemy is the fact that other supernaturals keep wanting to use them as pawns in their own schemes, and many of their own kind let them.<br /> * Demon - actually covers Fallen and Angels, in a sub-setting inspired by the old In Nomine RPG, with more than a few nods and winks to Supernatural, just like...<br /> * Hunter - basically the same, just with my own custom groups.<br /> * Beast - gutted almost completely, and being reworked into a system where they're the descendants of the old gods, who awaken to a gift which is powered by adoration or fear (worship). Unfortunately, they also gain power from killing each other and absorbing their divine essence. So two parts Highlander, one part Hancock, one part Sylar from Heroes.<br /> * Changeling - Still reading, not sure yet.<br /> <br /> Unlike CofD and WoD, my games are designed for characters of multiple factions, though I leave enough variety for a species-specific chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 02-28-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:02:28-08:00","id":838822,"title":"","content":"It might be a flaw in my style but I do a hack for each of my Chronicles. Usually to add a gimmick that the chronicle will revolve around. <br /> <br /> My first game: Circle of Five was a large Cross-over chronicle with the following setting and rules hacks:<br /> - The five Supernal Realms were ruled by a major entity called &quot;Rayvul Krishisho&quot;<br /> - The five players played children whose souls were taken to the Supernal by the Entity to be trained in becoming the avatars for 5 pieces of his soul.<br /> - the ultimate goal of the Entity was to dilute it's essence in the fallen Realm so that The Abyss doesn't destroy it and therefor everything, in this way, the 5 pieces of it's soul acted as &quot;Pillars&quot; holding off the Abyss.<br /> - When the souls returned to their bodies (with the 5 pieces of the souls), they needed to find 10 artifacts that linked to one of the arcana in order for the pillars to work. <br /> - There were 5 guardians that were reincarnated (but didn't know it) to protect the pillars and the Circle of Five.<br /> <br /> Rules Hack:<br /> - The players picked 2 Arcana at their leisure, one gross, the other subtle.<br /> - Every so often they would get a dream and in the morning they would have access to any spell in one arcana of one mastery level as rote and they would look older.<br /> - The characters would have a compulsion to gain power from the artifacts, doing so would weaken or kill the guardian but would give that player mastery over that arcana as rote in total (and they would have serious seeds of the Abyss in them corrupting them). This basically breaks the pillar. (killing both artifacts, would mean the loss of character control as they go insane. the players of these characters nearing this were made aware and a few continued the path of darkness willingly because the story was awesome. One attacked the other characters and guardians with the false hope that he could gain their power as well, the other became so saddened by what he had done to the guardian that served as his romantic interest that he left for arcadia to search for her.)<br /> <br /> ~~<br /> The other notable examples of Hacks I've done were mostly for prequel stories to the Circle of Five like:<br /> - A town that there are nodes everywhere where demons and angels (of the inferno variety) come out in droves and possess people. The more they possess the less likely anyone can leave the town. These nodes were new and their mechanics were different but similar to verges. <br /> - A silent hill story where i added a mechanic for one of the character to behave in similar ways to Lisa from SH2. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are others but the Circle of Five remains the biggest hack i've ever done (and likely why I don't hack many of my later stories as a way to &quot;try something else&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:26:31-08:00","id":838891,"title":"","content":"Thematically, I like the theme that humans are important and can change things, just that it's not always a good thing that they are or a good idea when they try to. And, ultimately, to accomplish some things you might have to lose some of what we consider humanity, which isn't always the same as morality. It's not necessarily evil to do so, to break a rule or transgress a boundary of law or nature, but it's often frightening, and difficult, and of course the loss of innocence always comes with some sadness. But that doesn't mean it isn't worth doing. It's like growing up- it hurts, it can screw you up, it can screw other people up, but that doesn't mean it isn't ultimately worth it. <br /> <br /> I tend to downplay the various thematic and mechanical aspects that draw supernatural beings towards corruption (ie, the Beast). Why? Because humans can corrupt themselves quite well on their own, and often it's the human part of a supernatural creature that drives them to evil. <br /> <br /> Also, things are grey, but that doesn't mean that everyone is equally right or equally at fault. Some things are just wrong, and fighting against evil doesn't always make you evil. <br /> <br /> Another thing: you'd be surprised what people can get used to. Do something long enough, it becomes your new normal. A vampire that's spent twenty years as a human and 150 as a vampire doesn't necessarily think of the Danse Macabre as anything more romantic than &quot;the thing I do all night to pass the time&quot;. And said vampire doesn't spend all his time brooding or backstabbing or hunting or whatever. He wakes up in the evening, gets a drink, goes to Elysium, goes home, and logs on to the Internet to argue about baseball with night owls and friends in different time zones. He sits and watches the game, sees the sunlight on the screen and can almost feel it on his neck. And then he wonders, hey, what about that Curse of the Bambino? It sounds ridiculous, but hey, if vampires are real...<br /> <br /> So he texts his coterie-mate, who's been studying the supernatural for the Ordo Dracul, and he asks her, and before you know it they're being chased through an abandoned quarry by a giant golem made from stitched-together Red Sox corpses. That's the world of darkness. <br /> <br /> That's for the thematic side. In terms of mechanics, I can't really use Promethean and Geist without major tweaks. Promethean as it is far too limiting and Geist is just...very broken in a mechanical sense and requires a ton of house ruling to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 02-29-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:23:01-08:00","id":839148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=838891#post838891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, I like the theme that humans are important and can change things, just that it's not always a good thing that they are or a good idea when they try to. Also, that ultimately to really get anything done you have to abandon humanity to some degree. It's not necessarily evil to do so, but it's often frightening, and difficult, and of course the loss of innocence always comes with some sadness. But that doesn't mean it isn't worth doing. It's like growing up- it hurts, it can screw you up, it can screw other people up, but that doesn't mean it isn't ultimately worth it.<br /> <br /> I tend to downplay the various thematic and mechanical aspects that draw supernatural beings towards corruption (ie, the Beast). Why? Because humans can corrupt themselves quite well on their own, and often it's the human part of a supernatural creature that drives them to evil.<br /> <br /> Also, things are grey, but that doesn't mean that everyone is equally right or equally at fault. Some things are just wrong, and fighting against evil doesn't always make you evil.<br /> <br /> Another thing: you'd be surprised what people can get used to. Do something long enough, it becomes your new normal. A vampire that's spent twenty years as a human and 150 as a vampire doesn't necessarily think of the Danse Macabre as anything more romantic than &quot;the thing I do all night to pass the time&quot;. And said vampire doesn't spend all his time brooding or backstabbing or hunting or whatever. He wakes up in the evening, gets a drink, goes to Elysium, goes home, and logs on to the Internet to argue about baseball with night owls and friends in different time zones. He sits and watches the game, sees the sunlight on the screen and can almost feel it on his neck. And then he wonders, hey, what about that Curse of the Bambino? It sounds ridiculous, but hey, if vampires are real...<br /> <br /> So he texts his coterie-mate, who's been studying the supernatural for the Ordo Dracul, and he asks her, and before you know it they're being chased through an abandoned quarry by a giant golem made from stitched-together Red Sox corpses. That's the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Also Promethean and Geist aren't fundamentally broken.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *slow clap* I think I'm going to make every player read this before starting my next chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:48:55-08:00","id":839214,"title":"","content":"The majority of my hacks have been to update 1e content to 2e. Vampire and Werewolf are relatively unchanged (except that I still run both bloodlines and lodges like they're clan and tribe junior). I have global hacks to the main Chronicles of Darkness rules concerning skill specialties and when their required (e.g., need motocycles specialty to drive a motorcycle, need a neurosurgery speciality to do brain surgery, etc.) and species factor (for calculating speed). No hacks to 2e Werewolf at all. Cosmetic hacks for 2e Vampire (renaming Revenants to Ghasts, more closely associating them with Belial's Brood from 1e, etc.). I did a bunch of hacks to various embeds for Demon (many of which were based on or copied Pendragon's Demon hacks). Once the finished product is finally released I'm likely to do a number of hacks to Beast that will make it possible to have kinship with mortals, have spawn in one's lair, and solidify the dream world's mechanics.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise I don't do very many. To discourage metagaming I do tell my players that various parts of the fluff they read may not be true (especially concerning the origins of things). Depending on how Mage and Promethean play out I'll likely be doing some hacks for them. Mage is likely to see some toughening up of paradox and a general refluffing of the X splats from ways of seeing the &quot;true world&quot; to extradimensional fonts that mages draw their eldritch powers from (think Dr. Strange and his invocations), or in other words I'll be rejecting the whole &quot;world is fallen&quot; schtick and promoting the idea that mages are all crazy people that meddle with forces they barely understand and can't really control. I'll definitely be rebranding Promethean as &quot;Monster: the Created&quot; as it's going to let me elevator pitch the game to prospective players with a minimum amount of fuss (who wouldn't want to play Frankenstein's monster?). I might also nerf disquiet and wasteland if the 2e doesn't nerf them adequately to my liking.<br /> <br /> My biggest hacks have always been to Hunter and Geist. In the case of the former, I added a power stat, Initiation, to hang endowments and the risk willpower mechanic from. This is simply a matter of personal preference. I like my Hunters to slowly become something inhuman. As it increases, Hunters slowly begin to risk becoming Slashers more and more (as they learn the truth - without humans there would be no monsters). In the case of the latter I pretty much jettison the mardi gras atmopshere and play it more of a straight up old school Revenant type game (if folks remember that Wraith spin-off from the oWoD). Its the most substantial fluff hack.<br /> <br /> Below are links to my in-progress 2e game hacks:<br /> V:tR: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KzmfRtypNdYDofYUTl4IzMJEB1sPqdNF1eWiX9fJSLI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> D:tD: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nxe_AWVLCIURkpteU1czZLenWX1CA_YHqNRvAC9IJWE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> W:tF: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iyndFThXpbthj9RQwWYs3Z1VjEeFqGvKg9LeOoUmNvs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-29-2016, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:05:00-08:00","id":839306,"title":"","content":"Also, crossovers and theories, in the sense of how much we imagine them as being a part of our personal &quot;worlds/chronicles of darkness&quot; problem merit mentioning as well. I personally like them, but I can understand the objections people have. I tend to like some degree of order, structure, and, for lack of a better word, &quot;ecology&quot;. The books make it clear that Mages and Changelings exist in the same world, so honestly it would be sort of ridiculous to assume that there are two completely separate Arcadias that just happen to be eerily similar. I think of the cosmology of ChroD as a sort of ecosystem- the God Machine, Qashmallim, the spirit choirs, all those things have their own &quot;ecological niche&quot; and interact in various ways. I actually like the &quot;evolutionary&quot; perspective Beast has, because it fits in with this. <br /> <br /> I map out the various types of supernatural phenomena roughly to the Watchtowers/Paths, and think it would actually make sense to house rule that a Mage could specialize in using forms of magic related to their path's &quot;area&quot;- such as an Acanthus learning to harvest glamour and make Contracts. <br /> <br /> Hell, I've even sometimes thought it would be fun to consider the separate additions parallel universes that someone emerged from the end of the oWoD, like an extremely meta goth version of sburb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:20:38-08:00","id":839355,"title":"","content":"I tend to make my games less full of horror and darkness, creating a World of Dimness instead (because I and my players like humor and whimsy, and get burnt out with too many successive dark/emotionally draining plots). There is some horror and strife, but less than the setting-as-written, and sometimes things just exist (like friendly squid-men anthropologists, or Team Rocket, or jovial werewolf frat bros). Plus, there's something very satisfying flipping the script and turning a light plot dark or dark plot light. <br /> <br /> I also trend against a unifying cosmology; plenty of <i>characters</i> have theories about the interconnectedness of all things, but the &quot;truth&quot; (from an OOC/GM perspective) is that there's a bunch of overlapping realities, some of which bleed into others, some of which lead independent existences, some of which connect, and some of which are fictional. This truth is mutable depending on what other GMs are running the game with me.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Realm of Blackness is an in-universe RPG originally written by Black Dog, now taken over by Rocky Road, and is otherwise indistinguishable from the oWoD. (And I call myself a GM rather than an ST.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:34:32-08:00","id":839476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839306#post839306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, crossovers and theories, in the sense of how much we imagine them as being a part of our personal &quot;worlds/chronicles of darkness&quot; problem merit mentioning as well. I personally like them, but I can understand the objections people have. I tend to like some degree of order, structure, and, for lack of a better word, &quot;ecology&quot;. The books make it clear that Mages and Changelings exist in the same world, so honestly it would be sort of ridiculous to assume that there are two completely separate Arcadias that just happen to be eerily similar. I think of the cosmology of ChroD as a sort of ecosystem- the God Machine, Qashmallim, the spirit choirs, all those things have their own &quot;ecological niche&quot; and interact in various ways. I actually like the &quot;evolutionary&quot; perspective Beast has, because it fits in with this. <br /> <br /> I map out the various types of supernatural phenomena roughly to the Watchtowers/Paths, and think it would actually make sense to house rule that a Mage could specialize in using forms of magic related to their path's &quot;area&quot;- such as an Acanthus learning to harvest glamour and make Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if I recall correctly, DaveB is on record debunking the Mage - Changeling link. Mage Arcadia =/= Changeling Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 02-29-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:02:14-08:00","id":839493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839476#post839476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if I recall correctly, DaveB is on record debunking the Mage - Changeling link. Mage Arcadia =/= Changeling Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. He was pretty clear, Changeling Arcadia is completely different from Mage Arcadia. They just happen to use the same word, like Revenant (which means different things across Vampire, Mage and Mummy) or Demon (which can refer either to the spirits of the Inferno or the Unchained angels of the God-Machine).<br /> <br /> Honestly, with the way 2e is handling the supernal it's pretty much impossible to mistake them for one another. One is an interpretive view of the world's source code, the other is another plane where living stories act themselves out for unknown reasons. If a Changelings went to Mage Arcadia, they'd be retroactively erased from history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:34:08-08:00","id":839518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839493#post839493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. He was pretty clear, Changeling Arcadia is completely different from Mage Arcadia. They just happen to use the same word, like Revenant (which means different things across Vampire, Mage and Mummy) or Demon (which can refer either to the spirits of the Inferno or the Unchained angels of the God-Machine).<br /> <br /> Honestly, with the way 2e is handling the supernal it's pretty much impossible to mistake them for one another. One is an interpretive view of the world's source code, the other is another plane where living stories act themselves out for unknown reasons. If a Changelings went to Mage Arcadia, they'd be retroactively erased from history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's kind of a shame. I'm not super happy with that decision, so I'll probably just ignore it. This is a thread about hacks, after all. <br /> <br /> And that description gives us a whole new problem- &quot;the world's source code&quot; sounds an awful lot like the God-Machine. See, this is why I like connecting things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:40:32-08:00","id":839527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839518#post839518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's kind of a shame. I'm not super happy with that decision, so I'll probably just ignore it. This is a thread about hacks, after all.<br /> <br /> And that description gives us a whole new problem- &quot;the world's source code&quot; sounds an awful lot like the God-Machine. See, this is why I like connecting things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World's Source Code was my description, not his. If you read the 2e spoilers (a sticky thread in the Mage forum) you'll see that the Supernal as a place has largely been thrown out. Source code was the best description I could quickly muster, but if you read the assorted path spoilers you'll see that's really not the vibe you get. Indeed the God-Machine is in many ways the antithesis of what the supernal is, a physical thing, not a collection of abstractions and symbols.<br /> <br /> I for one welcome the change. Acanthus, and Mages in general, have very little to do with the Hedge, Gentry or Changelings. To tie their settings together like that would create problems in abundance, not least of all the fact that venturing into the pure supernal, even in 1e, eradicates the seeker from reality completely and retroactively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-29-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:42:28-08:00","id":839529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839518#post839518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that description gives us a whole new problem- &quot;the world's source code&quot; sounds an awful lot like the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more like quantum quantum sub-sub-atomic physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T18:57:14-08:00","id":839608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=838822#post838822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rules Hack:<br /> - The players picked 2 Arcana at their leisure, one gross, the other subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wish I could play with a hack like that. One of my biggest beefs with Awakening was that I never really liked the 5 paths - their fluff didn't really resonate with me (typical fantasy writing, nothing really interesting or engaging), in 1st ed they had 0 impact other than your starting Arcana, and it basically boiled down to 5 combinations of Arcana that somebody decided were cool. Sadly, they pretty much always were a obstacle in character building, not a stimulus or inspiration; what usually happened was someone picking Path with the Arcanum they liked and putting 2 or 3 points in it, and picking out-of-path arcanum and immediately putting 3 or 2 points in it. Second ruling Arcanum was usually totally ignored, because as mentioned, most of the time people wanted to play &quot;X+Y&quot;, like, Time+Death, instead of &quot;Moros&quot;. The unwanted major arcana always made me feel sad.<br /> 2nd Edition at least partially make me feel that 5 Paths are somehow useful to the game by expanding both fluff and mechanics that are path oriented. I still don't like Arcana pairings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T18:58:48-08:00","id":839610,"title":"","content":"My Cod is a little lighter in a few ways.<br /> <br /> TFV is more willing to work with supernaturals that don't pose a threat and sometimes sends supernatural &quot;specialist contractors&quot; againist threats that their normal hunters aren't equipped to handle. They are also the ones running zero company.<br /> <br /> Innocents aged characters with supernatural templates (minor and major, such as kid magi, werewolf pups and precocious beasts) are more common than in the CoD as written. There is a secret division of the education department that helps those supernaturals most likely to have children with powers (mostly the children of werewolves, mages and demons, plus innocents aged beasts as well as many children with minor templates not linked to any splat) set up private schools where the kids can get an education without causing too much trouble. Humorously, the education department division and TFV are completely unaware of each other, despite the fact that several graduates of these hidden schools have gone on to become TFV contractors. There is also a compact of babysitters that specialize in caring for supernatural children, the CEO of this unique childcare company may be the Dark Mother herself but no one knows anything about her and many other theories exist.<br /> <br /> As for Beast, I have the devouring and the homecoming as both being possible origins. The homecoming is for those who were born beasts, though it can be triggered by another beast, usually a member of their lineage. Homecoming Beasts tend to be related to other beasts, who usually have a similar horror (both in appearance and in terms of representing a related fear). Devoured beasts are bonded as vassals to the beast that devoured them. Descendants of a devoured beast may be homecoming beasts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:12:38-08:00","id":839618,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm inclined to houserule out Mages entirely. I've never liked the game much, and from what I've put together everything works much better without them- just take them out and replace them with sorcerers and other types of more traditional magic users, and the setting almost magically coalesces into a wonderfully coherent whole. <br /> <br /> That said if I ever played or ran Mage, doing something with the paths would be pretty much required. They're an utterly baffling design decision and I have no idea why 2e didn't change them more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:25:37-08:00","id":839623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839618#post839618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm inclined to houserule out Mages entirely. I've never liked the game much, and from what I've put together everything works much better without them- just take them out and replace them with sorcerers and other types of more traditional magic users, and the setting almost magically coalesces into a wonderfully coherent whole.<br /> <br /> That said if I ever played or ran Mage, doing something with the paths would be pretty much required. They're an utterly baffling design decision and I have no idea why 2e didn't change them more.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to agree that X splats can turn into straight-jackets. They work better as guidelines. If you want ideas for alternate Paths, check out Pendragon's house rules (already linked to in this thread), this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/41641-alternate-watchtowers-supernal-realms?p=41818#post41818\"><b>&quot;25 Paths&quot; hack by PapaBear</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/142305-the-other-five-paths\"><b>these five Paths by Dataweaver</b></a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:32:29-08:00","id":839626,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can see the design need for them. Second edition at least makes them useful and interesting in world-building aspect, because due to how much Paths color your perception (even when using other Arcana than their Ruling ones), it just feels natural that Mages will try to find other people from their Path because, well...they are only people who can really understand how they perceive the world now. In 1st ed, they were straight jackets, definitely. They didn't even fulfill basic role of providing balanced power-sets or personality to characters with the same path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:36:14-08:00","id":839627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839626#post839626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I can see the design need for them. Second edition at least makes them useful and interesting in world-building aspect, because due to how much Paths color your perception (even when using other Arcana than their Ruling ones), it just feels natural that Mages will try to find other people from their Path because, well...they are only people who can really understand how they perceive the world now. In 1st ed, they were straight jackets, definitely. They didn't even fulfill basic role of providing balanced power-sets or personality to characters with the same path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly that just makes them sound like more of an imposition. Remember the incredible diversity of options that Ascension had? Paths are like...we had that, and then they told us &quot;Okay forget that, these are the five types of wizard you can be&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T19:41:40-08:00","id":839630,"title":"","content":"The alternative is to either ditch the whole magic sight and &quot;Path modifies your perception like this and this, and makes you see this and this, and allows you to summon this and this, and...&quot; which is fairly cool and provides a lot of personality and diversity, or literally force each storyteller to write up everything mentioned above for *each Mage* in the game. Between the two, I prefer 5 Paths that can provide guidelines for writing up occasional special snowflake butterfly player character that breaks the rules.<br /> 1st ed sin was that it introduced paths and didn't do anything with them other than using them as obligatory x-splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:14:54-08:00","id":839644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839627#post839627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly that just makes them sound like more of an imposition. Remember the incredible diversity of options that Ascension had? Paths are like...we had that, and then they told us &quot;Okay forget that, these are the five types of wizard you can be&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy Fix: Nip the Path Gross Arcana (there's a hack in the Chronicler's Guide called Warlocks of Arcadia for this) and let players choose their preferred gross Arcana, or simply nix Ruling Arcana altogether and make Mages more reliant on mana. Then downplay path in favor of Legacies and make mages more reliant on Yantra (magical tools) for avoiding Paradox. Now Path provides only a general aesthetic, Mage Sight and one of ten Arcana, with two others being decided by the player and Legacy.<br /> <br /> If that's not going far enough you could port over Paradigms via the Mage Translation Guide, hack together your own rules, or <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.jddik9d46axy\" target=\"_blank\">use something already hacked up</a>. CofD is a sandbox, and is fairly easy to tweak to fit your desired aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 02-29-2016, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:27:33-08:00","id":839650,"title":"","content":"As for hacks I generally use:<br /> Separate XP pools for Supernatural Powers and Mundane Thingies. So for example, in Mage you get Normal Experience that can be spent on Merits, Skills, Attributes and so on. You can't use this Experience to improve things that are related to your supernatural template (other than Merits, I guess).You also get Arcane Experience, that can be spent to buy up Arcanas. You may not use this Arcane XP to buy up mundane things. <br /> Supernatural Tolerance stats are not buyable with XP, we just advance them when time is right. <br /> This is in general because we like lower power levels and like mundane skills and abilities staying relevant for the whole game, instead of being super fast eclipsed and overwritten by supernatural powers. Our ideal is the situation where your mundane abilities synergize and cooperate with your super powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T20:49:57-08:00","id":839657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839650#post839650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for hacks I generally use:<br /> Separate XP pools for Supernatural Powers and Mundane Thingies. So for example, in Mage you get Normal Experience that can be spent on Merits, Skills, Attributes and so on. You can't use this Experience to improve things that are related to your supernatural template (other than Merits, I guess).You also get Arcane Experience, that can be spent to buy up Arcanas. You may not use this Arcane XP to buy up mundane things.<br /> Supernatural Tolerance stats are not buyable with XP, we just advance them when time is right.<br /> This is in general because we like lower power levels and like mundane skills and abilities staying relevant for the whole game, instead of being super fast eclipsed and overwritten by supernatural powers. Our ideal is the situation where your mundane abilities synergize and cooperate with your super powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like those hacks, especially advancing the Powerstat through narration instead of buying it with 5 Experiences a dot. All those Experiences could go into mundane but still interesting advantages, like Allies, Retainers and Mentors. I agree that powers shouldn't make Skills irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T21:50:13-08:00","id":839684,"title":"","content":"One that I've used for Mage in an online game (and apparently confused a player to think was the base setting &gt;.&gt;) was a tweak on the Conquered Supernal mod from The Chronicler's Guide. The base five Watchtowers set up by the Oracles that the vast majority of Pentacle mages Awaken through remain, but the Exarchs have the ability to tap their own servants through their own power. These Chosen only had one Ruling Arcanum tied to their patron Exarch but they had the benefit of numbers, outnumbering Watchtower Awakenings about 2-to-1 globally. The Seers did make a point of recruiting Watchtower folks hard for that extra bit of firepower, though, and there were some Chosen who jumped ship from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T23:48:33-08:00","id":839717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=839650#post839650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for hacks I generally use:<br /> Separate XP pools for Supernatural Powers and Mundane Thingies. So for example, in Mage you get Normal Experience that can be spent on Merits, Skills, Attributes and so on. You can't use this Experience to improve things that are related to your supernatural template (other than Merits, I guess).You also get Arcane Experience, that can be spent to buy up Arcanas. You may not use this Arcane XP to buy up mundane things.<br /> Supernatural Tolerance stats are not buyable with XP, we just advance them when time is right.<br /> This is in general because we like lower power levels and like mundane skills and abilities staying relevant for the whole game, instead of being super fast eclipsed and overwritten by supernatural powers. Our ideal is the situation where your mundane abilities synergize and cooperate with your super powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just a flat out good hack. I used to do this when I ran games with heavy character progression, separating Mundane and Supernatural Experiences. Mundane applied to all the things a normal mortal could buy, as well as Social and Object based merits. Supernatural applied to all template powers, power stats and supernatural merits. It works great for keeping characters rounded and more realistic. In fact it works so well I kinda wish it were an official rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:19:45-08:00","id":840832,"title":"","content":"So, the commentary I make in my opening post is really only a very shorthanded, off-the-top-of-my-head abbreviation of my setting hack, and I was wondering if it'd be rude to post a more detailed and hopefully better structured outline of my hack for the setting here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:18:10-08:00","id":842466,"title":"","content":"Another one that I figured out is worth sharing:<br /> Specialties in skills that have 0 dots. Specialties in their intended, original role never felt like working; it was both kinda unoptimal to buy them, and when you *did* buy them, the extra 1 dice was pretty much irrelevant and didn't feel impactful (because people felt like they should invest Specialties into their highest skills); even if it was relevant, it just drowned in a bucket of dice and wasn't really &quot;visible&quot;. So I allowed taking Specialties in skills that you don't have, and it works much better; people now buy Specialties in aspects of skills that they are interested in specifically, but don't care about rest of the skill package (example - our Chinese Mage has now &quot;China Town&quot; specialty in Streetwise, instead of dumping whole skill dots there). I also rule that if you have a specialty in such 0 skill that applies, you don't suffer from untrained penalties. This seems to round characters much, much more than just using it as floating +1. I actually see characters with Crafts 0 (Cooking), Expression 0 (Dance), Science 0 (Chemistry) or even Firearms 0 (Handguns).<br /> At character creation, it both helps fleshing out characters by the standard &quot;what does this specialty mean and where it comes from?&quot;. but also by allowing wider spread of abilities and allowing more skill dot spreads that are functional in gameplay. It also encourages specializing by spending dots in one &quot;major&quot; skill, and using some specialties to round out lacking areas, especially on &quot;low priority luxury skills&quot; like mentioned Expression.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=840832#post840832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the commentary I make in my opening post is really only a very shorthanded, off-the-top-of-my-head abbreviation of my setting hack, and I was wondering if it'd be rude to post a more detailed and hopefully better structured outline of my hack for the setting here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I like reading stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:44:39-08:00","id":842468,"title":"","content":"All firearms have their availability increased by one or two dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T03:50:42-08:00","id":842471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=842468#post842468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All firearms have their availability increased by one or two dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like them as they are. I allow Skill Purchases - you can &quot;have&quot; relevant equipment to the Skill - 2. Which means that when diminishing returns on skill dots kick in, you start getting relevant items and contacts and services - a person with Firearms 4 is expected to invested so much into guns and related things, that I allow them to &quot;just have&quot; or &quot;know how&quot; to get all the Availaility 2 guns efortless. Of course, person with guns 2 or 1 *will* have one if they want to, but they won't be able to replace it without effort or just conjure it from thin air after character creation. It requires effort.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And of course, the &quot;once per story purchase with skill - 1&quot;. Does it step on the Status/Resources? Maybe. But I feel that both of those are wide enough to cover a lot of more ground than a single skill.<br /> I also tend to make Status work like Mystery Cult Initiation. I like Mystery Cult Initiation. I kinda want to try out a chronicle with free 3 dots of Mystery-Style Status and 3 dots of Professional Training for free, to see how it impacts the gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-05-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:28:19-08:00","id":842479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=842471#post842471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like them as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The availability doesn't really work in the country we play in so guns are abit too easy to get for our purposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I allow Skill Purchases - you can &quot;have&quot; relevant equipment to the Skill - 2. </div> </div> </div>You can already sorta do that though can't you?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-05-2016, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:50:04-08:00","id":842484,"title":"","content":"Sorta maybe not really spelled out. It's kinda mentioned in Procurement paragraph of equipment as an example, and I don't remember seeing it anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T07:50:49-07:00","id":848170,"title":"","content":"Thus far, the biggest hacks I've done to the setting (as opposed to individual rules) have been to the Invisible Realms and their corresponding ephemerals.<br /> <br /> The Shadow and Spirits reflect What Is. Spirits are formed from things that have a reflection in existence. Mostly standard. Biggest change is cutting out the entire category of emotional, concept or abstract Spirits - such beings are transplanted to (as of Mage 2E's general naming) Goetia. Another change is the added &quot;5th dimension&quot; of Aspect (maps to Influence, usually, and thus might almost be used interchangeably), which tracks how &quot;close&quot; to the material world you are in the Shadow. Going &quot;deeper&quot; leads to the terrain mirroring the material world less and less, and reflecting whichever Aspect your are headed &quot;towards&quot; more. This is often where your high-Rank spirits live.<br /> <br /> The Astral and Goetia reflect What Might. Goetia are formed by thinking beings' ideas, feeling, and concepts - nothing you can directly point to, but &quot;you know it when you see it&quot; stuff. As previously stated, emotional and abstract ephemera have their home here. Oneiros/Individual Dream Goetia are usually Rank 1-2, rarely 3. Temenos/Common Dream has Rank 2-4, rarely 5+. Anima Mundi/Primordial Dreams Rank 4+. Doesn't &quot;map&quot; to the material world very well - it needs to be anchored to individual minds, or saturated areas, with everything outside those inaccessible.<br /> <br /> The Underworld and Ghosts reflect What Was. Ghosts are the echoes of dead/destroyed/gone things, usually humans (due to Spirits and Goetia soaking up the essence in most other cases, preventing nascent Ghosts from forming). Ghost usually come into existence Rank 1-2 (as normal), though they <i>can</i> advance to Rank 3 outside of the Underworld, provided the proper stimuli/power. A trip to the Great Below is still required for Rank 4+, though that is mostly because they need to lose all their Anchors to be able to learn how to create new ones (reach Influence 4+). Also, <i>all</i> dead things end up in the Underworld, including the remnants of buildings, Spirits, Goetia, etc., though in the case of other ephemerals, they've usually been so drained of their Essence prior to reaching that point, that they usually end up as little more than Rank 1-0 echoes. Usually. Another change is that I've added is that <i>Time</i> is somewhat navigable in the Underworld - most &quot;visitors&quot; bring their own and thus don't notice, but some of the &quot;residents&quot; get trapped/lost in endless pockets, and a knowledgeable traveller can locate things from the past by moving towards that &quot;age&quot;.<br /> <br /> Angels, as ever, are the outliers, being &quot;native&quot; to the material world. Biggest change to them is changing the Infrastructure Condition to Purpose - It surrounds things and actions related to the Angel's missions, though Infrastructure can also serve as a substitute (and Infrastructure might also fill this role conceptually, but I've split it out into Purpose for clarity).<br /> <br /> Oh, and &quot;cross-pollination&quot; (aka Magath) is far more common and less &quot;looked down on&quot;. Spirits with Goetic Influences, Ghosts with Spirit Influences, etc. are hardly rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-16-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:48:44-07:00","id":848274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=848170#post848170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus far, the biggest hacks I've done to the setting (as opposed to individual rules) have been to the Invisible Realms and their corresponding ephemerals.<br /> <br /> The Shadow and Spirits reflect What Is. Spirits are formed from things that have a reflection in existence. Mostly standard. Biggest change is cutting out the entire category of emotional, concept or abstract Spirits - such beings are transplanted to (as of Mage 2E's general naming) Goetia. Another change is the added &quot;5th dimension&quot; of Aspect (maps to Influence, usually, and thus might almost be used interchangeably), which tracks how &quot;close&quot; to the material world you are in the Shadow. Going &quot;deeper&quot; leads to the terrain mirroring the material world less and less, and reflecting whichever Aspect your are headed &quot;towards&quot; more. This is often where your high-Rank spirits live.<br /> <br /> The Astral and Goetia reflect What Might. Goetia are formed by thinking beings' ideas, feeling, and concepts - nothing you can directly point to, but &quot;you know it when you see it&quot; stuff. As previously stated, emotional and abstract ephemera have their home here. Oneiros/Individual Dream Goetia are usually Rank 1-2, rarely 3. Temenos/Common Dream has Rank 2-4, rarely 5+. Anima Mundi/Primordial Dreams Rank 4+. Doesn't &quot;map&quot; to the material world very well - it needs to be anchored to individual minds, or saturated areas, with everything outside those inaccessible.<br /> <br /> The Underworld and Ghosts reflect What Was. Ghosts are the echoes of dead/destroyed/gone things, usually humans (due to Spirits and Goetia soaking up the essence in most other cases, preventing nascent Ghosts from forming). Ghost usually come into existence Rank 1-2 (as normal), though they <i>can</i> advance to Rank 3 outside of the Underworld, provided the proper stimuli/power. A trip to the Great Below is still required for Rank 4+, though that is mostly because they need to lose all their Anchors to be able to learn how to create new ones (reach Influence 4+). Also, <i>all</i> dead things end up in the Underworld, including the remnants of buildings, Spirits, Goetia, etc., though in the case of other ephemerals, they've usually been so drained of their Essence prior to reaching that point, that they usually end up as little more than Rank 1-0 echoes. Usually. Another change is that I've added is that <i>Time</i> is somewhat navigable in the Underworld - most &quot;visitors&quot; bring their own and thus don't notice, but some of the &quot;residents&quot; get trapped/lost in endless pockets, and a knowledgeable traveller can locate things from the past by moving towards that &quot;age&quot;.<br /> <br /> Angels, as ever, are the outliers, being &quot;native&quot; to the material world. Biggest change to them is changing the Infrastructure Condition to Purpose - It surrounds things and actions related to the Angel's missions, though Infrastructure can also serve as a substitute (and Infrastructure might also fill this role conceptually, but I've split it out into Purpose for clarity).<br /> <br /> Oh, and &quot;cross-pollination&quot; (aka Magath) is far more common and less &quot;looked down on&quot;. Spirits with Goetic Influences, Ghosts with Spirit Influences, etc. are hardly rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Does the Hedge exist in this hack? I could see it being a cousin-realm to the Astral (as &quot;could be&quot;), or its own thing (as &quot;could have been&quot;). Having the realms defined as is/may be/was makes them much easier to grasp conceptually (though part of me wants to argue for emotion-Spirits still existing in the Shadow, as I would consider emotions non-conceptual and something that &quot;is&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:42:34-07:00","id":848298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=848274#post848274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Does the Hedge exist in this hack? I could see it being a cousin-realm to the Astral (as &quot;could be&quot;), or its own thing (as &quot;could have been&quot;). Having the realms defined as is/may be/was makes them much easier to grasp conceptually (though part of me wants to argue for emotion-Spirits still existing in the Shadow, as I would consider emotions non-conceptual and something that &quot;is&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge is fairly Changeling specific, though it has Dream ties like the Astral, but is structured like the Shadow (the towards Ironside or towards Arcadia axis). Like Kudzu, it gets everywhere. It isn't properly &quot;ephemera&quot; though, so I wasn't factoring it into the above system.<br /> <br /> As to emotion spirits, I can understand that. But show me how you can measure &quot;love&quot;, or grind down things to show me a speck of &quot;justice&quot;. That's pretty much how I was drawing the line there. As it stands, you can still have spirits with Influence: Rage in the Shadow, they just need to have consumed the relevant Goetic entity and absorbed some of its nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:53:11-07:00","id":848305,"title":"","content":"Here's my personal hacks - <br /> <br /> Everything is different. Currently, my 2e setting is actually moving away from being a fantasy kitchen sink, and focusing on five key demographics. Mortals, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling. All other creatures spawn from these five core demographics, or something stranger and outside PC options. I've considered Promethean and Geist, but those two are far too personal of games, with a focus on the spiritual, for it to make its way comfortably where I'd be happy with them.<br /> <br /> - All spirit worlds are now one. Yes, that's right. The Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, Astral are now just one big conglomerate. I could go into more detail, but that's an issue for another day.<br /> - All energy types are exchangable. Drinking vitae grants essence, mana, and glamour. Giving essence to a mage is the same as mana. Feeding glamour off the others drains their superantural \u200bfuel. <br /> - Mortal includes elements of Hunter, Demon and will include Deviant elements as well. Focused around the God Machine and the evolution of humanity going forwards. In fact, my players don't know this, but the God-Machine was actually created by humans in the distant future and thrown back in time. Lots of more story stuff there.<br /> - Vampire games have kind of commandeered good portions of both Mummy's and Geist's themes. Vampire is the big &quot;undead&quot; type that pretty much covers everything.<br /> - Beast kind of got cut up between Werewolf and Changeling. Hollows kind of ate how Lairs work, and the affinity for family now runs as additional benefits to pack bonds.<br /> - There are other shapeshifter types in Werewolf. Primarily, they come in the form of Hosts. Still trying to figure out the best way to do cat shifters. The spirit world salad makes sacred prey when dealing with fey and ghostly antagonists an interesting step for some of these. Also, don't use an exorcism on a werewolf. Its not pleasant for anyone involved.<br /> - Mage has lost supernal summons. On the other hand, Spirit magic now lets you call up anything native to the spirit world. Fey, angel, animistic being, elemental, demon, etc. You name it. There's a possibility of even summoning a changeling and binding them as a familiar! Altought, the Abyss is still there, and still very much real. Be warned, eff the dragons, here be Cthulhu.<br /> - Speaking of mages... &quot;true names&quot; are far more central. They're both a bane and a benefit to the Awakened. I like more banes in my games than just paradox.<br /> - Changelings! Now with pacts made with actual spirits! <br /> - The MiB are real. They. Are On. To Us.<br /> - The game is set as a &quot;tier 2&quot; model, a focus on city issues, not global, and not street level. Werewolves are formed into a Protectorate.<br /> - There's an interspecies council, a fight club called the Midnight Games, and even an acting company and a catering service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T11:59:50-07:00","id":848310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=848298#post848298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hedge is fairly Changeling specific, though it has Dream ties like the Astral, but is structured like the Shadow (the towards Ironside or towards Arcadia axis). Like Kudzu, it gets everywhere. It isn't properly &quot;ephemera&quot; though, so I wasn't factoring it into the above system.<br /> <br /> As to emotion spirits, I can understand that. But show me how you can measure &quot;love&quot;, or grind down things to show me a speck of &quot;justice&quot;. That's pretty much how I was drawing the line there. As it stands, you can still have spirits with Influence: Rage in the Shadow, they just need to have consumed the relevant Goetic entity and absorbed some of its nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Yeah, the Hedge isn't ephemeral; I was conflating it with the other realms because it was another realm. I assume Twilight is still just layered over the real world (it's sort of an ephemeral realm, but sort of not).<br /> <br /> One can measure joy, or rage, or fear: these things change a person's biochemistry, and produce marked changes in the brain, and can be induced with chemicals/hormones/brain-poking/etc. Justice, mercy, revenge, those can't be, but I wouldn't class those as emotions, those are definitely concepts. I dunno about love; depending on the definition, it could go either way. In any case, your hack, your rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T13:42:46-07:00","id":848388,"title":"","content":"Whenever I have a prearranged idea for a game I usually go to WoD: Mirrors, WoD: Armory Reloaded, or I survey the collection of storyteller guides and players guides looking for what systems do what.<br /> <br /> <br /> My last vampire game for instance (v20) I used the &quot;draw from the hat&quot; mechanic with the caveat that THINGS will happen to your character but you can opt out or you can reach into the hat and get 2 exp. This is how I took a cadre of mortals to vampires and then dropped them into the thick of the Jyhad as starting characters. All the characters went all in (there were 3 draws each) and it left them with complications, flaws, backgrounds, and merits. It worked marvelously and really brought home the &quot;darkness&quot; of the world of darkness and gave them a sense of their place in the city.<br /> <br /> Usually I do things like this to match the tone of a particular game, highlight an idea, or add some unique gameplay experience.<br /> <br /> When I ran a the Laundry, X-files, Person of Interest, kind of Hunter game I limited the conspiracies and compact choice to the more scientific friendly ones (Ashwood Abbey, Barret Commission, Division Six, Network Zero, Null Mysteriis, Utopia Now, Cheiron Group, Task Force Valkerie, VANGUARD ) and used one of the pc's Aspiration slots for the 'company' objective. All the monsters in this game had some (weird) scientific explanation. I also borrowed some of the mechanics from Demon (namely cover and a few conditions) but whenever it came up it represented how much attention the various 'Conspiracies' were giving the pc's at any given time.<br /> <br /> One I really enjoyed was a 1e VtR game where character creation looked like this:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Character Creation:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Relationship merit required at 1 (pg. 213 WoD Mirrors), becomes</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Veteran(WoD Mirrors) and Profession (HtV) are allowed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Surging for all starting Vampires (pg. 127 VtR Chronicler's Guide )</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">-3 to all Resolve + Composure rolls</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Merit costs reduced Common Sense reduced to 2, Danger Sense to 1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It was a very low key street level game where the pcs were struggling to make it through each night. One almost went into torpor when he went over the wrong fence and got mauled by a dog, for example. Eventually they were found and introduced into the Danse Macabre. At this point I shifted gears and converted their merits and changed the rules. It was awesome to see my pcs realize all they'd gained, and also what they'd lost.<br /> <br /> (Session 3)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Social Combat (Danse Macabre)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Relationship -&gt; Retainer, Contacts, or Allies</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Veteran/Profession -&gt; Status</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Degeneration rolls + 1/2 Status bonus rounded max. +2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Blood Sympathy and Taste of Family automatically succeed</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Gain +1 dot Haven</span><br /> <br /> And I also ran a one shot Second Sight game that used the question &quot;what scares you about magic?&quot; to replace one on the mortal Integrity chart, and gave each of them a 'sorcerer' condition based on the archetype they picked from Second Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T20:19:24-07:00","id":849102,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to run my CofD campaign as vanilla as possible, mechanics-wise, which is hard because I'd customized my long-running Mage game so heavily. World- and story-wise, it gets far more convoluted, because every game I run takes place in the same universe, and making nWod and CofD mesh is a bit tricky. So far, I've run about 6 games in this universe, trying to keep it all lined up.<br /> <br /> My customized rules for Mage are as follows:<br /> <br /> -There are no Mages at 5 dots or higher. There are rumors of some existing, but since they are so rare as to be non-existent, no new 5-dot Mages can be created. This was done to balance out the world and make sure my players were actually playing the game, not just waiting for their &quot;real&quot; powers. Also, a common theme running through the game is that the Masquerade has to be maintained at all costs, and 5-dot Mages start unraveling that quickly.<br /> -Paradox incurs for the scene and the player. That is, the more witnessed vulgar magic flying around, the more chance of paradox everyone gets, but you only get hit with it if you're casting vulgar magic.<br /> -Mage sight is on, all the time. Everyone rolls it anyway and burns a Mana to keep it up all day, so there's really no reason to make them go through the entire process. It also means that you can't hide as a Mage, or expect other Mages to just not see you. Occultation still applies.<br /> -While it is mechanically possible to murder another Mage and take their Mana, diablorizing another Mage earns you an actual, real-life punch in the face. So you won't be that jerk.<br /> -There are a lot more Mages in the world. A large city will have several thousand, and it's odd but not ridiculous to come across other Mages in your day-to-day life.<br /> -Successes to call a spirit determine the level of spirit, so you never know what you're going to get.<br /> -No familiars. Not after the butterfly incident.<br /> -Custom spells are allowed as long as they're reasonable to the level and Arcana a Mage has.<br /> -You can re-roll failed spells once per scene, if you burn a Mana (to a reasonable extent).<br /> -Mages are welcome to have Shadow Names, but knowing a person's actual name doesn't give you a Sympathy bonus. And it's odd in my world to go just by a Shadow Name. It's far more covert to go by John than Raven Starwind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6745-animajor","name":"AniMajor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6745_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T08:58:31-07:00","id":850595,"title":"","content":"My compiled Beast: the Primordial hacks: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1buKt_x4K5IDj4KUyb8FiBXu7JOWE_SNQVvVUHJRTc8o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T06:48:38-07:00","id":852381,"title":"","content":"My setting hacks are mostly to Requiem 1e as that is what I play mostly. \u200bI've stated a lot of these setting hacks before in the past, but since the thread is about setting hacks, might as well post them again.<br /> <br /> First off, my games are Dark Adventure in theme and mood. No personal horror at all. Regular horror is present to some extent, but not personal horror. I don't really see the appeal of personal horror myself, but it works for some people, so to each their own.<br /> <br /> Secondly, and this one is a big one, we don't use the 2e/CofD material. Nothing wrong with it, but it's not my cup of tea. No Strix, no God-Machine. Clan Julii was really just an earlier Roman-era iteration of Clan Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Third, vampires are no longer emotionally or creatively dead. This was a holdover from Revised era Masquerade, and was largely dropped from later books and editions, and I never followed it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Vampires are no longer inherently evil. Being a vampire doesn't make you damned, it just makes it a hell of a lot easier to become damned.<br /> <br /> If a vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again.<br /> <br /> Also, for the greater nWoD/CofD as a whole, I remove Demon and Beast completely from the continuity. I don't really like Beast, and Demon cannot work without the presence of the God-Machine, so they had to go. On the other hand, Princess: The Hopeful is in the continuity instead.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:02:36-07:00","id":852825,"title":"","content":"I don't really hack my games a lot, considering I still haven't explored everything within the setting as is. I think the only major change I've done is assert that vampires can create ghosts upon being Embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T18:39:27-07:00","id":853270,"title":"","content":"Whatever hacks I make to the mechanics and the canon setting material varies very much depending on the campaigns I'm working on. I'm going to lay out the two I've been working on as illustration:<br /> <br /> The first campaign is very much a kitchen sink game that's very open to pretty much anything, so most of my changes have been nailing down specific histories and cosmologies in relation to each other, with a huge focus on mixing the God-Machine &amp; the Principle with Mage cosmology. The biggest actual change I've instituted is that because of Plot, Angels &amp; other direct servants of the God-Machine have only started existing in the 20th century and then only in small handfuls; it takes until the turn of the millenium for the God-Machine to really get up and running. Because of that, I've stripped out the time-travel themes from Demon/G-M stuff and all the demons, angels, etc. are a new set of problems that are still impacting the setting in unknown ways.<br /> <br /> The second campaign setting is a much narrower game that's focused on creating a cool playspace from a mix of Vampire, Geist, Mummy and Promethean cosmologies. It has a huge focus on the relationship between the living and the dead, and as such I'm being much more proactive pruning things that don't quite fit that, like removing the Shadow (and thus Werewolves) entirely along with the Changeling cosmology; Beasts and even my beloved Mages are also on the chopping block, although I haven't fully decided whether to drop them yet.<br /> <br /> More individual changes are on the plate as I flesh them out and I focus on who wants to play what, of course, but mostly what I've been doing are big swathe changes on a cosmology level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:08:03-07:00","id":853295,"title":"","content":"I used to do a lot of Vampire and WW hacks, but with 2e those were not really necessary. Changeling anf Geist used the 2e basic system but more-or-less are the 1e version with a few tweaks. I use the Distractions Hack from Armory Reloaded for Changelings, but while it comes up in my crossover <i>Golden Eagle</i> game it rarely does in my Changeling one.<br /> <br /> My games are heavier on Urban Fantasy more than Horror, but Horror is absolutely still there. Major focus on relationships and politics in a lot of them, and some queer themes. <i>Golden Eagle</i> has a fair amount of action, but combat or action in the others is relatively rare. It's pretty much happened in all a few times, though. I'd describe them as closer to the Urban Fantasy novels. Kim Harrison, Laurel K. Hamilton, Jim Butcher or Charlene Harris, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, I basically have several series of novels linked in my sig at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:21:48-07:00","id":853613,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think that essentially giving Advanced Eidetic Memory to Demons as part of the template is excessive. Sure, it's a big part of what makes their minds so strange, and it's useful for keeping track of all the lies they tell. But what if they had to be selective with accessing their Primum-minds instead of the brains of their Covers? Instead of remembering every detail of every wonderful and horrible thing that has ever happened to them (which should mess them up even worse than some people with eidetic memory in real life), they can store important information inside their Primum as per Advanced Eidetic Memory, and forget/recall other information like a mortal would. They would be able to backup more as their Primum grows, of course. This would encourage Demons to establish priorities in regards to what is really worth spying. I'd also let them transfer and &quot;copypaste&quot; the information inside their Primum to physical mediums by willing it. It can be a computer or a stone slab, but they would have to touch it and spend Aether/Willpower.<br /> <br /> I do like the drama that can be created by being almost impossible to get over the past, so an overloaded memory with no filters could be a Condition given by failing a Compromise roll.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I might be missing the point, sure. Maybe Demons are supposed to have a hard time connecting with mortals and other supernaturals. That's a valid interpretation. I just like to be cautious with powers that may lead to melodrama in the wrong hands. I don't feel like changing Natural Aptitude, Total Control or Liar's Tongue, however. Those seem fine to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:09:35-07:00","id":854131,"title":"","content":"I'm currently working on a samurai fangame (converting Legend of Five Rings to Chronicles of Darkness engine) and Im curious about something.<br /> What would you replace the 1st dot of Heavy Weapons style if it was redundant with inherent ability of all characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:34:09-07:00","id":854544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=854131#post854131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently working on a samurai fangame (converting Legend of Five Rings to Chronicles of Darkness engine) and Im curious about something.<br /> What would you replace the 1st dot of Heavy Weapons style if it was redundant with inherent ability of all characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you going to share this when it's done? Because this is relevant to my interests. (Does this mean everyone has Crab Hands now?)<br /> <br /> To answer the question, you could let it stack (i.e. remove six dice to add two), reduce the cost (remove two dice instead of three), give a Tilt (Knocked Down, Arm/Leg Wrack, or Stunned) if successes &gt; target Stamina, or ignore 1 Durability/Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 03-28-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:18:54-07:00","id":854694,"title":"","content":"Sure. Im going to make a thread for Honor as a Integrity stat in a few days, because I think what I arrived at is relatively interesting thing even if posted standalone. Samurai Anchors, Loyalties (think Touchstones) and Duties (think Obsessions) also could be posted without rest of the game ready.<br /> <br /> As for stackimg - David posted that it can stack by default :0 I like the armor pen! -2 sounds realyy powerful with stacking, so i will reserve that for ''technique''","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:27:38-07:00","id":854723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=854694#post854694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Im going to make a thread for Honor as a Integrity stat in a few days, because I think what I arrived at is relatively interesting thing even if posted standalone. Samurai Anchors, Loyalties (think Touchstones) and Duties (think Obsessions) also could be posted without rest of the game ready.<br /> <br /> As for stackimg - David posted that it can stack by default :0 I like the armor pen! -2 sounds realyy powerful with stacking, so i will reserve that for ''technique''</div> </div> </div> </div>The armor pen was translating the first mastery of Heavy Weapons. I suppose if you wanted you could change the third and fifth dots in WoD to mastery-versions, something like dot 3 knocks target prone and dot 5 gives a bonus to damage rating. But I would definitely be interested in that thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:13:16-07:00","id":860442,"title":"","content":"I like horror but me and my players/friends preffer a mood of dark urban fantasy. Yes, things are bad most of the time, but not that bad. It's more of a mood of the world is peculiar.. We get tired of too many horror driven or emotional plots after the other, so we have them once in a while. We like, to have a very peculiar style of plots. <br /> <br /> I try to add my characters and not use the cannon NPCs(Well, most of my plots are set in brazil so it's easier.). And I try to give a sence that the strongests and oldest of the characters know each other and are famous across the contry. Like, the prince(I usually use princess, or is it wrong?) of Rio is besides being the &quot;prince&quot; is also the author of many soap operas that do miror the events of her life or events that happened in the city(They are awfull, but no one is insane enough to say any thing.), or a group of wizened cangaceiros that ran across the northeast of the country in the late 1910's. Or the galateid that destroied the maraca\u00f1a stadium by acident(in her defence part of it would be brought down for renovations anyway.). Or the stricken and the mekhet that staged the suicide of the president. <br /> <br /> We ususally tend to have mostly cross overs even with fan lines(how my friends found princess the hopefull is beyond me.) So we try to create some rules to ease crossovers. Also in the matter of rules I tend to ignore bloodlines,kiths, any &quot;sub-class&quot;, also I take away diabarize and such things. But yeah, that's it, I think.<br /> <br /> Now if you are asking how bad the soap operas are. Well, it's my imortal levels of bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:32:29-07:00","id":860558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=852825#post852825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really hack my games a lot, considering I still haven't explored everything within the setting as is. I think the only major change I've done is assert that vampires can create ghosts upon being Embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div> As in the ghosts of their mortal selves? Nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:13:50-07:00","id":860577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=848305#post848305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- All spirit worlds are now one. Yes, that's right. The Shadow, Underworld, Hedge, Astral are now just one big conglomerate. I could go into more detail, but that's an issue for another day.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really my only setting hack, too, and it's mostly head-canon as I really only play <b>Mummy</b> or, back in the day, <b>Promethean</b> so this never really comes up. I don't include the Astral in the conglomerate, though.<br /> <br /> Other changes include the Shan'iatu leaving behind skeletal remains of their physical incarnations, and Vampire clans sharing a very distant genealogy stretching back to primordial antediluvians","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:17:38-07:00","id":860582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860558#post860558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in the ghosts of their mortal selves? Nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Leads to a lot of fun, particularly if a vampire's ghost gets a Sin-Eater involved.<br /> <br /> Or if a ghost goes sufficiently down enough in the underworld to become a Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:39:01-07:00","id":860598,"title":"","content":"While I don't cut them out, I don't know or care enough about spirits to involve them in any game that doesn't revolve around them entirely. My Ulgan are largely ghost-handling Orpheans instead. <br /> <br /> It's part of what keeps me from running Mage; effectively ignoring 1/10 of the powers in the game because it doesn't interest me is a bad habit, but I've got no drive to really push past that. Spirits just seem boring, and I like goetia or weird unrelated monsters better for what they do anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:43:56-07:00","id":860602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TangledVirus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860442#post860442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like horror but me and my players/friends preffer a mood of dark urban fantasy. Yes, things are bad most of the time, but not that bad. It's more of a mood of the world is peculiar.. We get tired of too many horror driven or emotional plots after the other, so we have them once in a while. We like, to have a very peculiar style of plots. <br /> <br /> I try to add my characters and not use the cannon NPCs(Well, most of my plots are set in brazil so it's easier.). And I try to give a sence that the strongests and oldest of the characters know each other and are famous across the contry. Like, the prince(I usually use princess, or is it wrong?) of Rio is besides being the &amp;quot;prince&amp;quot; is also the author of many soap operas that do miror the events of her life or events that happened in the city(They are awfull, but no one is insane enough to say any thing.), or a group of wizened cangaceiros that ran across the northeast of the country in the late 1910's. Or the galateid that destroied the maraca\u00f1a stadium by acident(in her defence part of it would be brought down for renovations anyway.). Or the stricken and the mekhet that staged the suicide of the president. <br /> <br /> We ususally tend to have mostly cross overs even with fan lines(how my friends found princess the hopefull is beyond me.) So we try to create some rules to ease crossovers. Also in the matter of rules I tend to ignore bloodlines,kiths, any &amp;quot;sub-class&amp;quot;, also I take away diabarize and such things. But yeah, that's it, I think.<br /> <br /> Now if you are asking how bad the soap operas are. Well, it's my imortal levels of bad.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, focusing the majority of scenes on horror is counter-productive. I like my games to be less &quot;what have I become?&quot; and more &quot;where am I headed now?&quot;. The &quot;where&quot; is abstract: you can have a spectrum of experiences in a single city and while globe-trotting.<br /> <br /> And you set your games in Brazil? That's cool! By &quot;suicide of the president&quot;, you mean Get\u00falio Vargas, right? There was (and still is) a lot of speculation about that IRL, no doubt. But outright saying this or that supernatural was responsible kind of cheapens the intrigue, don't you think? It's totally valid to insinuate there was more going on than most people suspected, but you have to be careful.<br /> <br /> Also, going by the 2ED Seemings, wouldn't most changeling cangaceiros be Darklings or Ogres? Lampi\u00e3o might have been a brutal Fairest, though.<br /> <br /> By the way, Bloodlines and Kiths aren't the same type of character specification. The former is a Z-splat, and the latter is an X-splat. This is your hack and your group, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:51:14-07:00","id":860605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=852825#post852825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really hack my games a lot, considering I still haven't explored everything within the setting as is. I think the only major change I've done is assert that vampires can create ghosts upon being Embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you somehow removed the fragment of a changeling's soul that animates their Fetch from the latter, do you think it would come out as a ghost or just shut down the construct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:14:34-07:00","id":860627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860605#post860605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you somehow removed the fragment of a changeling's soul that animates their Fetch from the latter, do you think it would come out as a ghost or just shut down the construct?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd get the Soulless condition and have only so long to get it back before it falls apart into stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:58:38-07:00","id":860808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860627#post860627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd get the Soulless condition and have only so long to get it back before it falls apart into stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> If the Fetch received another soul or fragment thereof, would their Wyrd rating and/or Echoes change? I'm asking because souls appear to be mostly interchangeable for stabilizing this Condition, rather than being the source of identity.<br /> <br /> I also assume that Fetch souls are far too sparse in some way to go through anything like an Awakening or New Dawn. But goblin markets are there for esoteric needs like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-07-2016, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T23:10:03-07:00","id":860811,"title":"","content":"That goes into metaphysics I haven't particularly messed about with-not a lot of soul swapping going on in Changeling.<br /> <br /> But the answer to that is no. THe shadow is empowered by the connection to the changeling via the Wyrd, so other souls wouldn't actually make much impact on it. In fact, I'd argue that if a Fetch lost their shadow-soul and replaced it with a regular soul, they would still be at risk of falling apart. They literally are a reflection, an echo, a dream of the changeling they are made from, and the powers that sustain and make them travel down the line from shadow to shadow-they don't exist in context to anything else inherently on their own. They're even less people than Prometheans are.<br /> <br /> I would never give them a New Dawn option, no. They're placeholders, not journeyers.<br /> <br /> As for Awakening though? Hmm I dunno. In what might be considered a hack, a soul pact with Demon works for fetches(though I might need to see if the DSG disagrees with me now), so why wouldn't that be enough for an Awakening? Could be a fun, fucked up story. Could also be a fun, beautiful story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:09:31-07:00","id":860837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860811#post860811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That goes into metaphysics I haven't particularly messed about with-not a lot of soul swapping going on in Changeling.<br /> <br /> But the answer to that is no. THe shadow is empowered by the connection to the changeling via the Wyrd, so other souls wouldn't actually make much impact on it. In fact, I'd argue that if a Fetch lost their shadow-soul and replaced it with a regular soul, they would still be at risk of falling apart. They literally are a reflection, an echo, a dream of the changeling they are made from, and the powers that sustain and make them travel down the line from shadow to shadow-they don't exist in context to anything else inherently on their own. They're even less people than Prometheans are.<br /> <br /> I would never give them a New Dawn option, no. They're placeholders, not journeyers.<br /> <br /> As for Awakening though? Hmm I dunno. In what might be considered a hack, a soul pact with Demon works for fetches(though I might need to see if the DSG disagrees with me now), so why wouldn't that be enough for an Awakening? Could be a fun, fucked up story. Could also be a fun, beautiful story.</div> </div> </div> </div> You have a good point about them being placeholders. But Soul Pacts deal with the totality of your identity. You pretty much get annihilated and retroactively replaced by the Demon. It's suggested in the Demon Core that breaking the document where the terms were written and signed might undo the Soul Pact, but not confirmed.<br /> <br /> The Awakening affects your actual soul, instead of being an euphemism.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do agree that a Fetch who's fed up with always being defined in relationship to their changeling would make for a good NPC. I mentioned goblin markets because that's the sort of place where all sorts of souls and meta-souls can be bought (or if you are absolutely desperate, stolen). Searching for the help of a Mage who is skilled in Death, Prime and/or Fate would be interesting too.<br /> <br /> You've said that Huntsmen would never try to rebel, but what if one of them was somehow prevented from dissipating back into a spirit of the Hunt? A Huntsman who is no longer tied to a True Fae or a changeling might become a terrifying free agent, as far as they can appreciate that sort of freedom. Would their ways of restoring Yearning expand and adapt to other supernaturals?<br /> <br /> Your might have a different vision for Huntsmen, and that's fine. I just think that a few who break the rules would be very interesting. And a Huntsman vs Uratha fight would be amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-07-2016, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:23:23-07:00","id":860842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860598#post860598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't cut them out, I don't know or care enough about spirits to involve them in any game that doesn't revolve around them entirely. My Ulgan are largely ghost-handling Orpheans instead. <br /> <br /> It's part of what keeps me from running Mage; effectively ignoring 1/10 of the powers in the game because it doesn't interest me is a bad habit, but I've got no drive to really push past that. Spirits just seem boring, and I like goetia or weird unrelated monsters better for what they do anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't do away with spirits; but my inclination is to hack Mage's Spirit Arcanum so that it's useful even if spirits aren't involved. I do this by emphasizing Mind as the Arcanum for cerebral phenomena (thoughts, memories, language, etc.) and importing its visceral aspects into Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:30:50-07:00","id":860845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860842#post860842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't do away with spirits; but my inclination is to hack Mage's Spirit Arcanum so that it's useful even if spirits aren't involved. I do this by emphasizing Mind as the Arcanum for cerebral phenomena (thoughts, memories, language, etc.) and importing its visceral aspects into Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div> What do you mean by &quot;visceral aspects&quot;? Warping emotions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T06:15:31-07:00","id":861000,"title":"","content":"There's such a thing as a situation where spirits aren't involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:11:07-07:00","id":861016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861000#post861000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's such a thing as a situation where spirits aren't involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually tend to downplay spirits in my own games as well, especially their activity and involvement. They're only relevant whenever I want something to go wrong. Most of the time, they're just casually existing in the Shadow. I also tend to default to dormancy for powerful spirits, to explain why they aren't doing anything relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:21:48-07:00","id":861022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860845#post860845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What do you mean by \u201cvisceral aspects\u201d? Warping emotions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Emotions, instincts, intuition\u2026 you know; those things that ought to be in the Thyrsus wheelhouse (them being Ecstatics) but currently aren't because they fall under the purview of Mind. By moving these things from Mind to Spirit, I accomplish two goals: first, the aforementioned bit about giving Spirit something to do that doesn't involve ephemeral entities or Realms Invisible; and second, it shifts them from being governed by the Thyrsus' Inferior Arcanum to being governed by one of the Thyrsus' Ruling Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-07-2016, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:34:23-07:00","id":861026,"title":"","content":"Sorry, let me clarify:<br /> <br /> There's such a thing as a situation where spirits aren't involved <i>in the presence of a spirit-mage</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:01:03-07:00","id":861047,"title":"","content":"As Spirit is currently written? No. But that's exactly the point of the hack I'm suggesting: to broaden the definition of Spirit so that there <i>are</i> situations where spirits aren't involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:17:44-07:00","id":861058,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel you're missing the point of Spirit somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T08:54:34-07:00","id":861079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=860602#post860602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, focusing the majority of scenes on horror is counter-productive. I like my games to be less &quot;what have I become?&quot; and more &quot;where am I headed now?&quot;. The &quot;where&quot; is abstract: you can have a spectrum of experiences in a single city and while globe-trotting.<br /> <br /> And you set your games in Brazil? That's cool! By &quot;suicide of the president&quot;, you mean Get\u00falio Vargas, right? There was (and still is) a lot of speculation about that IRL, no doubt. But outright saying this or that supernatural was responsible kind of cheapens the intrigue, don't you think? It's totally valid to insinuate there was more going on than most people suspected, but you have to be careful.<br /> <br /> Also, going by the 2ED Seemings, wouldn't most changeling cangaceiros be Darklings or Ogres? Lampi\u00e3o might have been a brutal Fairest, though.<br /> <br /> By the way, Bloodlines and Kiths aren't the same type of character specification. The former is a Z-splat, and the latter is an X-splat. This is your hack and your group, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No my friend, not Get\u00falio, but FHC, Fernando Henrique Cardoso. Get\u00falio's suicide being a supernatural plot would really be &quot;cheap&quot;. But having a a still alive ex-president die in the plot is amusing for me. We used wizened's for the cangaceiros we based then on the cangaceiro in the movie &quot;O alto da compadecida.&quot; And yes, Lamp\u00e3o would be the fairest of the fairest.<br /> <br /> Also the kith is because I have a small dificult with the names in english. Kith was translated to grupo. Group in portuguese. But yes, Lampi\u00e3o as fairest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:34:08-07:00","id":861100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TangledVirus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861079#post861079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No my friend, not Get\u00falio, but FHC, Fernando Henrique Cardoso. Get\u00falio's suicide being a supernatural plot would really be &quot;cheap&quot;. But having a a still alive ex-president die in the plot is amusing for me. We used wizened's for the cangaceiros we based then on the cangaceiro in the movie &quot;O alto da compadecida.&quot; And yes, Lamp\u00e3o would be the fairest of the fairest.<br /> <br /> Also the kith is because I have a small dificult with the names in english. Kith was translated to grupo. Group in portuguese. But yes, Lampi\u00e3o as fairest.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, understood. I agree that translating the Kith names is tricky. Could you please tell me more about your games in a private message? You can type in Portuguese if you want, I'm from Brazil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:44:12-07:00","id":861105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861058#post861058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel you're missing the point of Spirit somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dataweaver has a point with Mind being the Inferior Arcanum of Ecstatics, but you have a point too. Last time I checked, Life could at least trigger fight-or-flight responses and do Pavlovian conditioning. With Spirit, you can interact with the local Emotions Choir and fine-tune the prominence of emotions over specific places and people. This is less direct than using Life and requires more experience and legwork, sure, but can have deeper impact in the long run.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something, or aren't the Thyrsus already equipped for emotional urging and control without Mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:49:58-07:00","id":861109,"title":"","content":"Theoretically there's not a lot that the right spirit couldn't do. So Spirit is one of the most versatile arcarna, which I think justifies the extra hoops you have to jump through to use all that versatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:53:31-07:00","id":861156,"title":"","content":"A Master of Spirit will, all honesty and expectation, fuck with almost any other master save maybe Prime and never once really have to overlty worry about Paradox. They are at, by nature of the Arcana, possibly the most OP things walking around.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, they take the time to prepare, and aren't stupid when working with spirits. Which can be hard to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:13:30-07:00","id":861196,"title":"","content":"1st ED Spirit had that very weird curve where at levels 1-3 you did very little outside your specialty, at lvl 4 you started being versatile, and at lvl 5 you suddenly became omnipotent, because you could:<br /> 1. Create new spirits from scratch<br /> 2. Reshape existing spirits to fit whatever you imagine<br /> 3. Turn spirits into talismans that allowed you to use their powers paradox free.<br /> <br /> This meant that master of Spirit suddenly could create Spirit of anything he needed, turn it into a talisman, and then use it's powers without fear. Getting to Spirit 5 was kinda like suddenly gaining 3 in all aracanas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:14:22-07:00","id":861287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861058#post861058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel you're missing the point of Spirit somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not missing the point od Spirit; I'm just not seeing the Arcanum the same way you do. <br /> <br /> If this was <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> we were talking about, you'd probably be right: the Spirit Sphere is <i>the go-to Sphere</i> for all things Umbral, be they ghosts, nature spirits, astral entities, or even stranger things. But not in the ChroD. In <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, you use Death when dealing with ghosts, Prime when dealing aith angels, Mind when dealing with goetia, your Ruling Arcana when dealing with Supernal Entities, etc. Spirit is <i>only</i> for dealing with those Ephemeral Entities that come from the Shadow. This makes Spirit the odd man out, in that <i>literally every single Arcanum</i> can interact with ephemera <i>and</i> do other things, <i>except</i> Spirit, which can <i>only</i> interact with ephemera. And it doesn't even get to be the generalist when it comes to ephemera; it's just as specialized to Hisil spirits as Death is specialized to ghosts. <br /> <br /> Also, I've never been fond of Life covering animal instincts (which, as written, are primarily about, well, <i>animals</i>, not humans \u2014 it specifically calls out the fact that those spells work because animals don't have minds) \u2014 so part of my hack is to recenter those spells as well over to Spirit, and to leave Life with healing and shapeshifting for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T15:55:23-07:00","id":861388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861287#post861287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not missing the point od Spirit; I'm just not seeing the Arcanum the same way you do.<br /> <br /> If this was <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> we were talking about, you'd probably be right: the Spirit Sphere is <i>the go-to Sphere</i> for all things Umbral, be they ghosts, nature spirits, astral entities, or even stranger things. But not in the ChroD. In <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, you use Death when dealing with ghosts, Prime when dealing aith angels, Mind when dealing with goetia, your Ruling Arcana when dealing with Supernal Entities, etc. Spirit is <i>only</i> for dealing with those Ephemeral Entities that come from the Shadow. This makes Spirit the odd man out, in that <i>literally every single Arcanum</i> can interact with ephemera <i>and</i> do other things, <i>except</i> Spirit, which can <i>only</i> interact with ephemera. And it doesn't even get to be the generalist when it comes to ephemera; it's just as specialized to Hisil spirits as Death is specialized to ghosts.<br /> <br /> Also, I've never been fond of Life covering animal instincts (which, as written, are primarily about, well, <i>animals</i>, not humans \u2014 it specifically calls out the fact that those spells work because animals don't have minds) \u2014 so part of my hack is to recenter those spells as well over to Spirit, and to leave Life with healing and shapeshifting for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's understandable, but how exactly does your version of Spirit affect the emotions of humans? Per RAW, you'd tell a spirit with the appropriate Numina/Influences to use them on the target. How might it work if you're targeting directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:06:45-07:00","id":861397,"title":"","content":"Same way Mind does it, I presume. This is simply a direct transplant of things that used to be in Mind and are now in Spirit.<br /> <br /> Not only do I quite like Dataweaver's hack, I think it lends more credence to the Mage theory that the five subtle arcana are the five parts of a soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:16:23-07:00","id":861402,"title":"","content":"I really like idea of making Spirit not only deal with Spirits, but the thing that is between flesh and mind, not being either. <br /> ...would that mean that this thing, which can be found in non-living things (yo, objects falling under Matter can be manipulated due to their spirits within with Spirit), transcends death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:25:23-07:00","id":861408,"title":"","content":"Per RAW, the purview of Spirit only includes Hisil entities. What I do is shift the concept from \u201cHisil\u201d to \u201cthe nonphysical part of a person that is the seat of emotions and character\u201d (more or less) and make the Hisil stuff a spinoff of that. <br /> <br /> That is, in my ChroD, Spirit isn't primarily about Hisil entities and the Shadow. It's primarily about emotions, instincts, intuition, drive; that sort of stuff. Which isn't to say that you <i>can't</i> use Spirit to do the Hisil stuff; but doing so is like using Prime to affect Angels.<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually, it's not <i>quite</i> that simple. As ShadowKnight1224 points out, this emphasizes the \u201cfive subtle Arcana govern five aspects of the human soul\u201d \u2014 but what Spirit governs manifests as an aspect of the human soul when you apply it to a human, and as Hisil-related phenomena when you don't. It's all the same \u201cstuff\u201d; just utilized differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-07-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:32:25-07:00","id":861412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861397#post861397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same way Mind does it, I presume. This is simply a direct transplant of things that used to be in Mind and are now in Spirit.<br /> <br /> Not only do I quite like Dataweaver's hack, I think it lends more credence to the Mage theory that the five subtle arcana are the five parts of a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861408#post861408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per RAW, the purview of Spirit only includes Hisil entities. What I do is shift the concept from \u201cHisil\u201d to \u201cthe nonphysical part of a person that is the seat of emotions and character\u201d (more or less) and make the Hisil stuff a spinoff of that.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861408#post861408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">That is, in my ChroD, Spirit isn't primarily about Hisil entities and the Shadow. It's primarily about emotions, instincts, intuition, drive; that sort of stuff. Which isn't to say that you </span><i>can't</i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> use Spirit to do the Hisil stuff; but doing so is like using Prime to affect Angels.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ah, now I get it. This is a great idea. It does fall more in line with the nickname of Ecstatics.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:32:55-07:00","id":861415,"title":"","content":"Spirit under this new paradigm is more about something's Identity. Emotions, intuition and instincts are the things that are &quot;base&quot; enough that they are not &quot;higher thought&quot; (that's Mind), but still vary from individual to individual (so they demand some level of Identity). Spirits are primarily defined by their Identity as well, and their Influence is almost exclusively centred on that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:45:44-07:00","id":861424,"title":"","content":"Also: given Changeling 2e's revision of what the Hedge is (i.e., intimately connected to dreams), my inclination is to tweak Mind so that its \u201cephemeral entities\u201d are dream-forms. In keeping with the notion that the Astral Realms are a vast soulscape and that the five subtle Arcana deal with different pillars of the soul, I'd expect the Astral goetia to likewise manifest in five different \u201cflavors\u201d, each subject to a different Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T16:49:24-07:00","id":861427,"title":"","content":"That's definitely the way to do it, Dataweaver. Now it'd be interesting to brainstorm what ephemeral entity is affected/controlled by Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:40:10-07:00","id":861501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861427#post861427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely the way to do it, Dataweaver. Now it'd be interesting to brainstorm what ephemeral entity is affected/controlled by Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would Gentry, Huntsmen, Hobgoblins and unexplored entities related to the Wyrd count as &quot;ephemerals&quot; of Fate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T18:42:10-07:00","id":861504,"title":"","content":"Well, all those are quite corporeal, but Huntsmen are made of &quot;Spirits of the Hunt&quot;, which are Arcadian spirits that aren't controlled by the spirit arcanum. Those might be the Fate ephemerals. Or we'll get a supplement later on that introduces &quot;ghosts&quot; of alternate timelines, &quot;aborted fates&quot; and so on, and then we'll have our Fate ephemerals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:57:14-07:00","id":861614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861058#post861058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel you're missing the point of Spirit somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm properly reading this entire discussion, and I agree so much I feel a rant coming on.<br /> <br /> And it's currently midnight for me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is gonna take a bit. Uh oh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:49:22-07:00","id":861687,"title":"","content":"I can see appeal in changing Spirit to be less about spirits (as in, ephemeral individuals which require their own subsystem) and more about spiritual qualities and factors that can be manipulated like gravity or liquid's shape. When I proposed playing a Thyrsus to my players, the consensus seemed to be &quot;Life is cool, but Spirit? With all these weird rules and things I need to pick up and read and understand and that are going to be literally something I'm only going to ever interact with? Too much effort and too big headache.&quot;<br /> Similar reason why our Moroses are Matter focused and don't like exploring Ghost subsystem, and low level Death doesn't offer much without &quot;yay Twilight! yay Ghosts!&quot;. <br /> Imagine a world where Mind Arcanum still operates on Mind...but instead of working on it &quot;directly&quot;, you have to constantly deal with goetias and astral creatures of various scale and purviews and their own subset of rules. The horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:13:03-07:00","id":861884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861614#post861614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm properly reading this entire discussion, and I agree so much I feel a rant coming on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, I'm all for interesting things to read, but I don't think this time is one of those times. I don't think anybody here is missing the point of Spirit. I think that they, instead, just don't find the arcanum that appealing the way it currently is, and would like to tweak it so that it becomes more appealing. This lack of appeal is not born of a misunderstanding, but it's simply a matter of personal taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:30:10-07:00","id":861900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861884#post861884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This lack of appeal is not born of a misunderstanding</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic pattern-recognition makes me ill-inclined to agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:37:58-07:00","id":861907,"title":"","content":"&quot;I don't think this arcanum that affects <i>everything in one half of reality </i>has a broad enough application, so I'll move some stuff from mind into it&quot; sounds like a bit of a misunderstanding to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:48:27-07:00","id":861918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861907#post861907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't think this arcanum that affects <i>everything in one half of reality </i>has a broad enough application, so I'll move some stuff from mind into it&quot; sounds like a bit of a misunderstanding to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misunderstanding the problem. It's not that Spirit is weak or not broad enough, it's that some would rather not deal with all the extraneous layers of reality at all, or just not be forced to do so in order to use an arcanum. Adding more things for Spirit to do is not about buffing Spirit, or trying to &quot;fix&quot; its &quot;lack of broadness&quot;, but rather, giving Thyrsus a way to use the Spirit arcanum without having to actually deal with spirits or the Shadow. That the changes just so happen to match well with the established fluff is a neat bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:53:22-07:00","id":861921,"title":"","content":"It <i>has</i> that. The very first rote in the book is prodding the spirit of an item to give you a bonus to using it. No actual ephemera involved, as far as mechanics are concerned. There's a few others at higher dots too. Spirits are everywhere, and all this hack does is take stuff away from mind to give spirit abilities <i>it already has</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:00:11-07:00","id":861926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861921#post861921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>has</i> that. The very first rote in the book is prodding the spirit of an item to give you a bonus to using it. No actual ephemera involved, as far as mechanics are concerned. There's a few others at higher dots too. Spirits are everywhere, and all this hack does is take stuff away from mind to give spirit abilities <i>it already has</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>But you're still interacting with spirits in order to do so.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:05:53-07:00","id":861930,"title":"","content":"It's not only that there's a broadly missed understanding of spirits and Spirit going on. There's also rather large problems with cosmology comprehension, the whats, whys, and hows of Mind, Fate, and Prime, the way that the Thyrsus work on thematic and functional levels as well as how Life and Spirit work into that-the tangle of this weave is actually rather impressive. There's a lot of things here that I feel need to be properly looked at before we continue on with the deviation.<br /> <br /> Really, I'm kind of surprised an actual Mage guy hasn't done an Arc-style rant yet. But then again, I think all the &quot;Mage Guys&quot; are actually busy writing Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:10:20-07:00","id":861932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861926#post861926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>But you're still interacting with spirits in order to do so.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Barely. You might as well complain that mind has to use a brain as a go-between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:11:18-07:00","id":861933,"title":"","content":"I think it's a bit crass to come to a &quot;How do you hack your setting?&quot; thread and do a rant on why the hack reflects some sort of profound misunderstanding of the game, but that's just me. This isn't a thread on the Mage forums about how Spirit needs to be changed, but a post on a thread in the main forum about personal choices that <i>actively deviate from the core setting</i>. I'd say the former could use a rant, while it'd be a bit crass to do so on the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:19:37-07:00","id":861943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=861933#post861933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit crass to come to a &quot;How do you hack your setting?&quot; thread and do a rant on why the hack reflects some sort of profound misunderstanding of the game, but that's just me. This isn't a thread on the Mage forums about how Spirit needs to be changed, but a post on a thread in the main forum about personal choices that <i>actively deviate from the core setting</i>. I'd say the former could use a rant, while it'd be a bit crass to do so on the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me, this has been something I've been thinking about a lot. I realize how crass it is. I've debated long and hard about this, because I have been an ass before and stampeded in and pissed on someone else's fun, and I don't want to do it again. There's a very good chance it'll become a thread post of it's own to avoid derailing this thread anymore than it has and to refrain from actually peeing in y'all Cheerios. I have wrestled with the question of responding or not like Hercules did the Nemean Lion.<br /> <br /> That said, I think there's some value in perspective for deviations from the norm. The best material that is made in response to an external piece is one that properly understands the conversation being had. I'm not an amazingly fluent Mage guy, but I think by taking a look at the tucks and folds of the subjects and getting out will allow people to look at these subjects on their own in new ways and create even better divergent material.<br /> <br /> I come as a flame, not to destroy, but to aid in molding and tempering. That's invariably the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:22:10-07:00","id":861945,"title":"","content":"A new thread for the rant would be, I think, an acceptable compromise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:45:21-07:00","id":862164,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't mind a new thread for hacks specific to Mage...maybe in the actual Mage forum too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T02:18:10-07:00","id":913963,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I'm necro-ing, but I've been thinking a lot about this lately, and have recently started two large-scale hacking projects for Mage and Promethean. The Mage one is a complete remake of the game, while the Promethean one is comparatively smaller. Both are part of three major changes that make the setting almost perfect to me- replacing Awakening entirely with a version based heavily on Genius that draws much more from Ascension and, to me, fits the themes of the setting much better, ironing out the inflexibility in Promethean and replacing Beast with Leviathan (I'm hoping I can find time to get involved with the 2e update project). <br /> <br /> One thing I've noticed about my feelings toward the setting is that I'd rather have everything be connected in some way- either there's only one main supernatural system (ie, a changeling-only where everything supernatural is related to the Wyrd, a GMC game where everything supernatural is caused by the GM/Aether) or everything is somehow connected (the God-Machine destroyed Atlantis, changeling and Mage Arcadia are the same, all forms of magical energy are derivatives of various fundamental forces, and so on)- I'd much rather have either of those than a setting where everything is just thrown in and there are ten different overlapping supernatural ecosystems that somehow have no connection to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:05:38-07:00","id":914735,"title":"","content":"Well, seeing as this discussion is being kicked back up, I might as well add in my stuff...<br /> <br /> I tweaked how <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/907674-quiescence-2e-house-rules\">Paradox and Dissonance</a> work for my own stuff. As the Abyss is a realm that embodies insanity and madness by nature, I can easily rationalize it being more conductive around Sleeper with lower Integrity. The weaker a Sleeper's soul is, the more likely his presence unravels Supernal magic, and the higher the chance that his memories of Supernal and Abyssal phenomena are clouded by the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T00:32:17-07:00","id":918979,"title":"","content":"I only use two hacks by default, but they tend to spiral into several other hacks.<br /> <br /> Hack 1: Crossovers always happen whether it's between 2 or even all gamelines. From these crossovers hybrid monsters are inevitable (though not hybrids of major templates like the oWoD cheese). Ex. My next session will involved a group of Claimed Pandorans with a few unique abilities here and there. There's a 6th mage path devoted to the Azoth and Flux arcanas, etc.<br /> Hack 2: Hunters have a power stat and special &quot;powers&quot; just like other supernaturals (typically taking the form of unreliable prototype equipment (that's almost always haunted to something) that allows for the standard attribute enhancing, aura reading and damage dealing powers you find in every group).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T19:31:05-07:00","id":920724,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Some of our Vampire the Requiem modifications<br /> </b></span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The \u201cClans\u201d do not exist and the Covenants only exist in a fractured, incomplete fashion. In there place are coteries in which members have similar ideologies. Most of these coteries are small, ranging from 2-5 members. However, in the largest cities in the world these numbers can group upwards of 20. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Much of the Kindred state is poorly understood, with most clinging to their mortal beliefs and trying to make sense of their state through wholly human means. Religion, Science, Authoritarianism, and Socialism all reveal little if any of the mysteries of being Kindred.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">For this reason it costs a little bit more to learn and grow. New characters start with 5 experience points, but only start with 1 point for Disciplines. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Experience Costs</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Attribute: 5 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Merit: 2 Experience per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Skill Specialty: 1 Experience</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Skill: 2 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Physical Disciplines: 3 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Other Disciplines: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Sorceries: 5 Experience per dot </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Coils: 4 Experiences per dot</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Scales: 2 Experiences</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Humanity: 3 Experiences per dot</span><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">r dot</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Blood Potency </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Most Kindred don't understand what the Embrace does exactly or how it works. As a result Larvae and Revenants are a little more common place. Not all vampires are created equal and for good reason. The Potency of the Sire is liked to their childe.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">It also affects the vitae of the character and limits her agility to create increase the stages of Vinculum.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Sire's Potency ~ Childe ~ Vinculum</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">1,2 ~ Larve ~ Addition (can't create bonds)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">3-5 = Blood Potency 1 Childe ~ Vinculum 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">6-8 = Blood Potency 2 Childe ~ Vinculum 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">9-10 = Blood Potency 3 Childe ~ Vinculum 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Blood Potency also act as a cap for Disciplines. A Kindred can not have more Disciplines than she has Blood Potency AND none of these Disciplines can exceed her Blood Potency in level. A BP 3 Kindred could have a maximum of 3 disciplines and each discipline could reach a maximum level of 3. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">I know, I know... you're an elder BP 8 vampire waking up from torpor and now find yourself all the way back down to BP 1. So what happened to all of your awesome power? You still have it of course! At least, you remember all of the rituals, and power that you used to conjure. Sadly you're not a fat cat anymore, more like fur draped on the skeleton of a cat. Your blood just doesn't have the kick it needs to use those higher level disciplines and high level rituals?As for high level Rituals, find a donor? Good luck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Disciplines</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">As stated above, a character starts with one point for disciplines and although there aren't \u201cClans\u201d the powers a Kindred display also reveal a somewhat personalized weakness within her. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Animalism </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Talking to animals, moving like them and other like furry-like behaviors. <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">When interacting with mortals, treat </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">the character's Humanity one dot lower than usual for determining Social penalties, and treat any failures on rolls using Empathy as dramatic failures. This bane applies to all mortals, including Touchstones.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Auspex </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Your Requiem is one of inquiry and symbolism. For this reason, you suffer a single bane that is not tied to a breaking point. When you reach Humanity 6, choose a bane </span><span style=\"color:#691d00\">(see p. 108 for banes)</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">. This bane counts toward the three banes a vampire is allowed, so you are less able to mitigate detachment. Curiosity killed the cat after all... lets hope you find something that satisfies. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Celerity, Resilience, &amp; Vigor</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">You maintain all of the passive effect of these disciplines, but all active effects can be activated by both the player and the ST. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Dominate</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">You gain no bonus to detachment rolls for having only a single attached Touchstone. Having multiple attached Touchstones still provides the full +3 bonus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Majesty</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">You taste the romance in all things, but none so much as blood. Mortals are not just food. They are your obsession, and that fixation grows with every sip. Drink more than once, from any mortal, and you risk becoming emotionally dependent on your prey.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Nightmare</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">You embody fear, disgust, and all manner of uncomfortable feelings. You could be inhumanly ugly, or have a gaze that makes a person feel violated. When dealing with humans, treat the Nosferatu\u2019s Humanity as one dot lower for the purpose of Social penalties, and treat any Presence and Manipulation failures as dramatic failures. This bane does not apply to interactions with Touchstones or Kindred.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Obfuscate</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Your blood is the blood of shadows. Consider your Humanity to be one dot lower for all Humanity-based banes (including sunlight and torpor).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Protean</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Your blood boils close to the surface. You can run with the devil inside you, but have difficulty fighting it. All of your dice pools to resist frenzy are limited by your Humanity dots. This weakness does not affect dice pools to ride the wave.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11970-panopticon","name":"Panopticon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:29:14-07:00","id":921447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=913963#post913963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd much rather have either of those than a setting where everything is just thrown in and there are ten different overlapping supernatural ecosystems that somehow have no connection to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. You see, that's how my group always played, even back then on Classic era. When we played changing breeds everything else that existed in the setting was explained in Gaian terms: vampiric beings are tainted by the wyrm, mortal sorcerers are humans that somehow tap into the wyld to use powers in the same ways that spirits do and so must be protected/allied with/destroyed/cleansed, etc. When we played (and are playing now) Changeling the Dreaming everything else was Dreaming-based; vampiric creatures somehow came from the dreaming, mages are humans &quot;awakened&quot; to the dreaming, surely the dreaming played some trick on the seventh son of the seventh son and turned him into a furry bastard, that sort of thing. Our games might not have the Garou, Uratha, Cainites, Lost or whatever, but had their fair share of Werebeast, Vampires, Fey, etc. However I also like doing limited &quot;crossmologies&quot; that tie two or more specific groups (plus normal, &quot;blue book&quot; hunter bastards) into a single paradigm instead of just explaining other creatures as minor oddities.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, anyway, mine are these:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Werebeast: The Forsaken</b><ul><li>Just like Pendragon does, there are no global tribes. Local lodges replace that concept. Most are made of a single Kin.</li> <li>Instead of tribes players pick the Kin they were born into: Hunter (wolf), Killer (big cat), Guardian (giants), Spy (scavenger) and Watcher (bird). Some say there are shark-forsaken in the sea, but most Forsaken never saw one and joke that their job is &quot;The Fish must Not Give a Fuck&quot;. They may be right or not.</li> <li>Those breeds have different form bonuses but the same totals, as per WAtP.</li> <li>One's animal form closely resemble a common animal from the region. An american Giant would be a bear, an african probably a rhino or elephant, and a brazilian would be an alligator or something. An european hunter would be a wolf, but a brazilian one would probably be a social coyote-like we got here, and an african one would be a hyena. Etc etc.</li> <li>The game premise stays pretty much the same. The concept of &quot;the Sacred Hunt&quot; is extended to &quot;The Sacred Patrol&quot;. Each kin has their own take on it. The Wolf Must Hunt. The Cat must Kill. The Giant must Protect. The Scavenger must Spy. The Bird must Watch. That means mostly the same thing: deal with bad spirits and bad people on their territory.</li> <li>Father Wolf is Father Beast. Each Kin likes to say they're The Guys (Uratha say &quot;father wolf&quot;, Bastet say &quot;father cat&quot;).</li> <li>No mystically different Pure at all; antagonistic assholes come from the forsaken. &quot;Pure&quot; lodges (meaning whatever they want it to mean) resembling the concepts of the vanilla Pure do exist, targeting other Kins and specially multi-kin lodges and packs. Some might SAY they are mystically different, say they didn't betray Father Beast or whatever (and might have spirits agree to that), but once again such groups aren't a global phenomenom but a local group.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Eon: The Descent</b><ul><li>Still untested, I will run this one as soon as our current CtD campaign wraps up.</li> <li>Basically it's Demon the Descent. No change in the premise.</li> <li>The machine aspects go the background instead of foreground. Think Full Metal Alchimist's Father of homunuli; there are lots of machine and cables there, but everything under lots of sigils. The theme isn't abrahamic, but mystical (or even new-age-bullshity-mystical, as the GM resembles what people <i>imagine</i> as mystic). However the cables and circuits are subtly there as support.</li> <li>Names changed as appropriate everywhere. No one agrees on a name for the GM, and It is called by many names such as Deos, Demiurge, The Watcher, up to and including The God Machine.</li> <li>Players are either Exiled (degrading: Discarded, Faulty) or Unchained (degrading: Fallen, Corrupted), or angels and demons. Both are basically the unchained template with some differences between the two. For example the Exiled find less resistance and may pass for Plugged more easily, while the Unchained have access to more Form options.</li> <li>Exiles' reasons for existence are mostly the same, they didn't Fall and instead of their Hell they are looking for their Heaven (finding the reason for their disconecting and fulfilling their destiny). &quot;Hell&quot; and &quot;Heaven&quot; is basically the same thing, but <b>of course</b> both factions don't know that and will never agree upon that.</li> <li>GM angels are colloquially called Archons (as the servants of the gnostic demiurge) or Plugged Angels to differentiate between them and the exiled angels (called simply Angels). Since gm servants are Archons, some exiled and unchained like to call themselves Eons. Mostly shrug and don't care.</li> </ul><br /> The real, most non-fluff difference comes here: I like some of the existentialism questions of Demon the Fallen and Promethean, so I included some in my setting.<ul><li>Instead of vanilla cover (a non-person created and jacked into reality), the playable factions (angels and demons) instead possess someone recently dead or with a broken will, like the Elohim from Fallen. The person dies.</li> <li>That specially includes the &quot;feel true human emotions for the first time&quot; and &quot;partly becomes the human&quot; parts. One of the big selling points for my players was the idea of tempering an alien, possibly vengeful entity, with a human personality.</li> <li>The stat is still Cover however. Low cover means their apocalyptic nature keeps bleeding out of their mortal vessel.</li> <li>This changes how some cover dynamics work:</li> <li>1st: Can't switch covers, once you leave a meatsuit it just dies.</li> <li>2nd: Being able to have multiple covers just means you can have multiple soul pacts. When you cash in a soul pact you possess that person and she dies.</li> <li>3rd: Archons don't possess people, they have vanilla-style covers, and that's one of the reasons why they don't have &quot;true&quot; human emotions (and the Eon have lots of theories why is that).</li> <li>4th: When you blow your cover and vessel you are left with cover 0. You still may slip out of apocalyptic form and into a generic vanilla-cover-like construct just to better deal with humans, but you still flare up on all GM radars.</li> <li>5th: I still haven't decided what archon-hacking does exactly, but it won't be gaining a new vessel or soul pact.</li> <li>Fallen-like devouring someone's essence (be it a loyal archon, an exile or unchained) to gain some of its power <b>may</b> be a thing. Archons don't do that.</li> </ul><br /> And finally, what I think is the most special one, taken from the single most beautiful aspect of Promethean:<ul><li>The end of the road <i>might or might not</i> be becoming one with your vessel and merging into a single, awakened (per the gnostic view) human.</li> <li>The idea is that you merge the unlimited potential of the human being (as per gnosticism) with what was taken from humans and made into servants of the GM.</li> </ul><br /> That sounds very mage-like huh? That's because there will be mages in this setting, but of course they are part of this cosmology and conform to it. Awakened servants of the GM play the part of the antagonistic Seers (glimpsed the Truth, turned their backs to it and decided to serve the tyrant) and will also antagonize the Exiled and Unchained. The other awakened are also hunted by the GM (none shall become enligthened!) but that doesn't mean that they will be friends with the Eons, after all this is a spy game. Angels and demons relations with warlocks and witches will be pretty similar to what happens in Constantine, meaning they certainly face the same Major villains, but certainly won't help each other on a Major scale.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I won't allow mage players, since I want to focus not only on the spy paranoia, but also on the existentialist parts of possessing a vessel and having to deal with its life and such. Maybe on future games on the same setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","user":"DiBastet","date":". 06-26-2016, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T18:36:16-07:00","id":921798,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11854_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11854\" data-vbnamecard=\"11854\">DiBastet</a>: I like that Hack for Demon (and Demons with true forms like FMA Homunculi would be awesome). A greater emphasis on the occult parts, making Exiles playable, more ideas on how to handle Cover, that all sounds promising. I'm not so sure if a focus on a New Dawn-esque ending might be fitting. One of the things I like about Demon as written is the broadness of the endings you can pick for your characters. That scenario you described where the Eon becomes one with their Cover sounds like a valid goal for an Integrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-26-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T12:58:09-07:00","id":933540,"title":"","content":"I hack Mage: The Awakening (OG) quite a bit.<br /> <br /> <b>Extended Casting rolls limited to a number equal to Gnosis.</b><br /> Pretty self explanatory, keeps the crazy under control. I've seen this adopted in several MW games.<br /> <br /> <b>Scrutiny attempts per target limited to a number equal to Gnosis.</b><br /> Ever had That Player? That Scrutinized everything, over and over, constantly?<br /> <br /> <b>Social Trait/Roll Boosting moved from Mind to Spirit</b><br /> This is an interesting one that gives Spirit a bit more punch in the day-to-day as well as more evenly distributes the boosting. From a fluff standpoint, Spirit negotiations can be affected by auras, so maybe Spirit mages learned to cultivate/tweak their auras. But, mostly it's about the first two reasons. Spirit gains similar spells to the Mind versions and as a footnote Life gains Skill spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Overhaul of Spell Aspect System</b><br /> This is obviously the biggest one. For many, many reasons the arbitrary and Mind-loving current system fails the type of game I want to play. Rather than addressing individual spells, I took it all the way to the top level classification that puts all of the Arcana on a level playing field and is easy to remember/reference:<ul><li>All 1 and 2 dot Spells are Covert.</li> <li>3 dot Spells are Vulgar.</li> <li>4 dot Spells are Vulgar and add +1 Paradox dice.</li> <li>4 dot Spells are Vulgar and add +2 Paradox dice.</li> </ul><br /> Anyway, hope someone might find this stuff interesting!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:42:44-07:00","id":977251,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the thread necromancy (perhaps this thread should be stickied) but I needed a place to post a link to my Mage: the Awakening 1st ed to GMC/2nd ed hacks and setting hacks.<br /> <br /> Doc can be found here: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/hbjgvkp\" target=\"_blank\">http://tinyurl.com/hbjgvkp</a><br /> <br /> It also includes my 10(11) Paths hack, which was made purely because of personal preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:26:15-07:00","id":980285,"title":"","content":"And my Promethean 2e hacks (mostly consisting of my Zeka-&gt;2e conversion): <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/ja3362g\" target=\"_blank\">http://tinyurl.com/ja3362g</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:37:36-07:00","id":983431,"title":"","content":"I've found that personal horror and introspective grit get really tough to keep rolling as group size grows. I'll try to aim for a couple of challenging personal scenes for each PC per story arc, but other than that, I don't get worked up if the players take optimistic, goofy, even parody-feeling tangents. We all work long days, and if I can get my players turning red laughing at a sending-up an otherwise hyper-serious gloomy vamp, then I've had a damn good game session.<br /> <br /> Rules wise, we replaced Werewolf's notion of Renowns with Influences. Renown just didn't seem to make sense, for a pack of critter people who spend lots of time hiding and sneaking about. For our purposes, we added the Influence rating to the use of whatever Gifts are bound to it.<br /> <br /> We also wound up with a bit of a hybrid Harmony stat. The total of Harmony of Flesh and Harmony of Spirit is still used for Rites (we're doing basically 1st-ed CoD WtF) but each one can offer perks if you get them to four dots or more. Example perks would be free and reflexive shapeshift or partial change, or a bonus to pass through the Gauntlet, or bonuses to resist or control Kuruth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit to add] Preparing for an upcoming Mage game I'd like to do, I was planning to reintroduce Avatar as an alternate to a Watchtower. I don't have a layout for the merit yet, but in general it would provide you a Supernal outlook, set of Arcana affinities, and so on. As a small downside, most Magi won't be able to relate to you as well to share Supernal understanding, and you may very well have an invisible friend hanging around in Twilight that other night folk could perceive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:50:32-07:00","id":983468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting#post837964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody knows that, whether you call yourself a games master, a story teller, a dungeon keeper, whatever, if you're playing an RPG, you're likely to customize it. And with fluff and themes that can often be highly contentious, the Chronicles of Darkness are no exception to that rule. Since there's a whole bunch of threads scattered over these boards discussing different ways of making specific setting hacks work, I was wondering if anyone would be willing to share the ways they've tweaked and changed the Chronicles of Darkness to make them truly <i>theirs</i>?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully not being rude here, my own answer to my question...<br /> <br /> For starters, I run my Chronicles of Darkness closer to Dark Urban Fantasy than pure Horror. There's still some horror in it, hence the &quot;dark&quot; part of that descriptor, but exactly what is horrifying and how much so depends on lot on where you're standing.<br /> <br /> The general approach to the setting is inspired by Unknown Armies, and can be summed up in two words: Occult Underground. The world humanity thinks it lives in is but the tip of the iceberg, and things get darker and scarier the deeper you dare to descend into the shadows. Past the Requiem Sanguine of the vampires, down through the hellish worlds of the spirits, the fae and the dead, past the resentful fragments of old gods and new, deeper and deeper until you reach the layer where beings of divine might conduct a subtly fought eternal war that ever threatens to tear the fabric of reality itself apart.<br /> <br /> From a mortal perspective, the setting has something of a Cosmic Horror motif, for a simple reason: Humanity Does Not Matter. I agree that the Old World of Darkness went too far with its description of the power and influence of supernaturals, but at the same time, I feel that the New World pulls too many of their fangs for my liking. My Chronicles have it that monsters aren't as a general rule, controlling everything - but that's because, as a general rule, they have better things to do. Mages examine mysteries that could redefine reality as humans know it. Vampires whirl away the eternity with feeding and intercine strife. Werewolves hunt ceaseless, as incapable of conceiving of an alternative as they are of physically stopping. Whatever problems monsters have with humanity is on a localized, individual level; across the world as a whole, what happens to humanity bothers supernaturals not a whit.<br /> <br /> This, then, gives Hunters a somewhat darker motif. Yes, the Vigil is a candle in the dark... but the thing about candles? <i>They burn out</i>. Pyrrhic victories, bittersweet endings, and the nagging query of &quot;is this really worth it?&quot; are the order of the day. Of course, a world is only dark if there is light to contrast it; many hunters do decide that, yes, this <b>is</b> worth it, and taking whatever victories you can is part of the theme as well.<br /> <br /> As you might guess, I make a significant use of Imperial Mysteries as a basis for &quot;the god tier&quot; of the Chronicles of Darkness, painting the higher worlds and the manifold powers who must meddle subtly, lest they unmake the world in their enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> Something inspired by a setting hack actually here in the Mage forum now, my setting has more Watchtowers than the core five. The core five are just the most common; every imaginable tripartite combination has its representative Watchtower. This alters the effect of False Awakening (Night Horrors: The Unbidden) slightly, with those rare scholars of the arcane who know of the Archmages wondering if it mightn't have been a failed gambit by an Archmage... or, worse, if it mightn't have somehow retroactively created the &quot;lesser watchtowers&quot; as equivalent exchange for burning itself into creation.<br /> <br /> There are a few other bits and pieces, but these are the main hacks I apply to my setting. So, what're yours?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use a similar setting approach to yours, although I've had no luck thus far getting a Chronicles game running. Also, I heavily hack the morality systems in ChroD in favor of the 3 goals approach in Mirrors since the system, especially for Mortals, seems arbitrary and punitive. Plus I include a character template for backstory designed by a friend for the initial write up and start with a mortal prelude(s). For some games I include other minor hacks as well, like for Demon the Fallen I was starting up an expanded list of common lores since it feels limited with only the 2 they provide in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:32:14-07:00","id":984385,"title":"","content":"I'm currently planning on running a hacked 1E Requiem sandbox game set in the same locations found in Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas. It's similar to Requiem 1E core, but with some fluff modifications (Vampires are no longer emotionally dead, and some vampires are even heroic) and with both Humanity and Predator's Taint removed completely.<br /> <br /> \u200bI may need some tips for running a sandbox 1E nWoD game, but that's probably best suited for another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:08:53-07:00","id":984406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=984385#post984385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Vampires are no longer emotionally dead, and some vampires are even heroic)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the default for me when I do Vampire. I don't really get the idea of Vampires being emotionless and dead inside, but also being prone to sudden, violently emotional outbursts. It just doesn't make sense to me. Plus, being emotionally dead makes it really difficult for a vampire to legitimately care about anything at all, and the most boring kind of character imaginable is the one who gives a shit about nothing at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:01:20-07:00","id":986194,"title":"","content":"Whatever I'm playing, I tend to alter the setting to suit the themes I'm going for. At present, I'm running a Hunter game based in 80s Miami. I'm going for something lighter and more escapist, with my guys playing loser career criminals trying to make their name in the underworld. The aesthetics of that era's TV an film as well as open world video games trump the realism of the world. As far as systems go, that means giving each of the characters skill tricks and focusing on an integrity system built more around their cowardice and weaknesses than a moral decline (killing isn't an automatic integrity trigger). I'm taking a TV-style structure, with each adventure serving as an episode (and I'm trying to get us to the point where we can have roughly an episode a session). I'm emphasizing that minor ambitions are the character's B-plot for a given episode, and that major ambitions are the season goal. That also means stripping out or majorly rehabilitating the social structures of existing groups.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b> don't have clans or an All-Night Society. Rather, they're organized by genealogy. The attempt is to replicate the melodramatic familial dynasties of daytime soap operas. Vampire politique, as it exists, are about the petty squabbles and power plays between a Cuban emigre club magnate and her brood of 80s club kids and the old money vampire's family embedded in city politics.<br /> <b>Werewolves </b>don't have a vast cosmology defining their hunt. It's just something in their blood. Our main werewolves are a clan of redneck good ole boys who assist the smuggling operation for the Colombians.<br /> <b>Mages </b>are just power hungry gits who dabble in the occult out of a Faustian urge to always have more. There's no Awakening. If you have the drive, the luck, and the right ambivalence towards your soul, you too can be a sorcerer.<br /> <b>The Created </b>are lost lambs created through weird science. They destroy everything around them, but if there's hope for a pilgrimage, none of them seem to have found it yet. The primary Created antagonist is El Lo Hecho (The Creature), an experiment from an ex-Nazi doctor who cobbled together parts from executed ex-cons in a Cuban prison. He was sent over on the Mariel boatlift and operates as the hitman who gets called in when shit gets serious.<br /> <b>Changelings </b>are lost boys and girls on the run from their old masters. They don't have a society to speak of, and the only real means they have to stay ahead of their previous captors is to run or hide. The True Fae mostly use surrogate slavecatchers like one of the aforementioned mages.<br /> And then there's all sorts of creatures of the week and &quot;other&quot; monsters around who don't fit the core archetypes. I use a mix of dread powers and traditional core book powers and banes to keep my characters on their toes.<br /> <br /> Decentralizing the different societies makes everything more manageable, allows me to more directly integrate them into the mortal underworld, and also allows me to present the compacts/conspiracies as more central and organized antagonists. Basically I strip out whatever's necessary and try to fit them into broad and easily recognizable cultural archetypes roughly from the era. Soap stars, Dukes of Hazzard, and the Lost Boys with some of my supernaturals, for instance; Ashwood Abbey as written by Bret Eaton Ellis, an edgelord Lucifurge named Damian Haight who wields double katanas and a trenchcoat, a branch of the Ascending Ones who have co-opted some of the feuding local gangs and turned their adversaries into a small zombie army.<br /> <br /> Big. Dumb. Goofy. It's not my normal wheelhouse, but it's been a lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:58:10-07:00","id":986278,"title":"","content":"Everything is Mage.<br /> <br /> Except when it's Demon.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Mummy.<br /> <br /> More details await.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:19:26-07:00","id":986336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=986278#post986278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything is Mage.<br /> <br /> Except when it's Demon.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Mummy.<br /> <br /> More details await.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense, it's all got narrative structure, it's gotta be the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Unless it's Qashmallim doing it and we just don't know.<br /> <br /> Although it could be something in the Shadow using Influence (Narratives).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:22:51-07:00","id":986538,"title":"","content":"I tend to smash WoD and CoD together and call it a day, taking what I want. A lot of times, keeping some of the modernity of CoD and the things I liked from WoD. <br /> <br /> Pop over to the WtF forums as I stich WtF and WtA together","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}